# Risk register
| Risk | Probability | Impact | Trigger | Mitigation | Fallback | Owner |
|---|---:|---:|---|---|---|---|
| Candidate portal weather and multiworld mods do not operate together | Medium | Blocker | Launch failure crash missing world or invalid destination | Test the minimum stack in an isolated 1.20.1 profile and pin exact versions | Replace only the failed component after preserving evidence | Luan |
| The asymmetric R4-to-R0 view and R0-to-R1 entry cannot coexist live | High | Blocker | R0 entry returns to R4 or another unintended destination | Test both faces and every entry direction before full construction | Use shot-specific portal configurations or composited destination plates | Luan |
| R1 weather is absent or incorrect through the R0 opening | Medium | High | Rain light or waterfall differs before and after crossing | Test weather without shaders and record static and lateral views | Composite a separate rainy R1 plate | Luan |
| Portal state changes after save and reload | Low–Medium | High | Destination orientation shape or direction changes | Record commands configuration IDs and orientation and preserve a known-good backup | Rebuild shot portals from the recorded setup | Luan |
| Camera replay shader or recording tools conflict with portal rendering | High | High | Crash clipping missing interior or corrupted replay | Establish a minimum-stack baseline and add one tool at a time | Capture without the conflicting tool or composite locked plates | Luan |
| Portal performance is too unstable for repeatable motion | Medium | High | Frame-time spikes chunk stalls or inconsistent parallax | Preload chunks reduce recursion and remove shaders | Capture foreground and destination separately | Luan |
| Echo geography drifts | Low if controlled | High | Ravine seam cave or surface profile differs | Derive every echo from one verified master and coordinates | Build a matched hero-location shell for required shots | Luan |
| The clean master or another echo is contaminated | Medium | Blocker | Files are copied in the wrong direction or destructive work reaches the master | Use explicit labels and verified milestone backups | Restore from the last master-derived backup | Luan |
| MATCH PATH drifts | Medium | High | Camera height field of view line or motion differs | Record one numerical transform and reference overlay | Use locked plates and rebuild visible dressing around them | Luan |
| MATCH FRAME A cannot be repeated exactly | Medium | Blocker | Moss position equipment light or pack action differs | Protect the established R0 state and record all marks | Reuse the Scene 2 image continuation where editorially feasible | Luan |
| The repeated narration is recorded twice | Low | High | Timing inflection or room sound differs in Scene 13 | Record one final performance and place the same asset twice | Replace both placements from one approved master | Luan |
| The granite seam becomes unclear or symbolic | Medium | Medium–High | Dressing or framing obscures its forked natural profile | Preserve a neutral master reference across echoes | Add a short orientation insert without lore | Luan |
| Wild-wolf and skeleton blocking is unclear or unsafe | Medium | High | Paths collide or the wolf appears tamed early | Test in a sacrificial copy and divide the action into passes | Join threat intervention and taming through controlled editing | Luan |
| Fishing capture depends on uncontrolled luck | High | Medium | Scheduling stalls or the catch is unreadable | Plan a controlled catch and inventory insert | Preserve fishing as the scripted cause through editorial continuity | Luan |
| Moss's name or collar appears early | Medium | High | An incorrect entity or world state reaches capture | Maintain separate wild tamed-unnamed and named states | Replace the plate from the correct state | Luan |
| Moss loses ownership name pose or AI state during crossing | Medium | High | Moss fails to cross duplicates or changes state | Repeat follow and sit-release tests before and after reload | Capture Moss destination-side and conceal the handoff | Luan |
| Fire does not follow the intended rug-to-timber route | High | Blocker | Spread stalls accelerates or destroys the evidence | Test the exact backed-up room geometry repeatedly | Use progressive controlled states with the same visible burn fan | Luan |
| Destructive capture removes the only lived homestead | Medium | Blocker | Fire wall breaking or blast occurs without a verified restore | Duplicate and verify the state before every destructive test | Restore the latest verified pre-fire copy | Luan |
| The edit resolves Moss's fate | Medium | High | A death message body collar-like drop or locating sound appears | Suppress messages and inspect every background item and sound | Remove and replace the affected plate or audio | Luan |
| Creeper route is invisible on rewatch or too obvious initially | Medium | Medium–High | The edge cannot be found or becomes an announced reveal | Review the sub-second plant at delivery size without a sting | Adjust framing duration or contrast only | Luan |
| Creeper landing and hiss cannot interrupt at the required instant | Medium | High | It misses lands early or fails to ignite behind the protagonist | Test route height landing mark and timing separately | Capture fall landing hiss and reaction as separate plates | Luan |
| Blast does not kill the protagonist while preserving readable geometry | High | Blocker | Damage is insufficient or destruction obscures the frame | Test difficulty equipment distance and damage in a sacrificial chamber | Use the black-frame fatal cut and an art-directed aftermath | Luan |
| Aftermath items look artificial or reveal forbidden evidence | Medium | Medium | Items appear impossibly or include Moss-related evidence | Base placement on tests and inspect every item | Use a restrained continuity-approved item plate | Luan |
| Delayed activation is mistaken for vanilla behaviour | Medium | High | Production or publication language presents it as factual | Label the effect as invented canon in every review | Rework effect language and release notes | Luan |
