{"summary":"Deepened Production for all thirteen draft-03 scenes with a provisional, explicitly untested Minecraft Java 1.20.1/Fabric baseline, deterministic take-control design, 49-panel text storyboard, implementation and test matrices, camera paths, locations, assets, budget, risks and planning-only build log. Exact 1.21.1 intersections cannot be established from the supplied primary-source evidence and remain a research blocker rather than an inferred compatibility claim.","document":"# Production plan — The Portal That Nobody Made\n\n> Research-first Production proposal for authoritative Script `draft-03`. Everything below is planned work. It does not evidence installation, interoperability, testing, completed builds, generated storyboard images, capture, selected takes, technical success, rights clearance or creative approval.\n\n## Authority and scope\n\n- This plan covers exactly one video, `The Portal That Nobody Made`, in Production.\n- `03-script/script.md`, draft `draft-03`, controls all thirteen scenes, chronology, causality, continuity, narration meaning, portal topology and Moss’s unresolved R4 fate.\n- Direction and Story material is informative only where it agrees with the Script. Superseded fixed-timeline, older-self-builder and wolf-rescue material must not enter Production.\n- The editorial guide remains 20:38. Individual timings guide coverage and do not impose a formula.\n- Public-facing language uses British English. All business figures use BRL.\n\n## Evidence vocabulary\n\n| Label | Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| Researched fact | Supported by an official or primary source recorded in the source ledger |\n| Documented individual support | A release page lists the stated game version or capability; no combined-stack conclusion follows |\n| Provisional recommendation | A preferred next test based on available evidence, not an approved toolchain |\n| Planned test | Procedure and acceptance criteria exist, but no result exists |\n| Verified result | Requires retained logs, exact artefacts, settings and review evidence; none exists yet |\n\nAll candidate stacks remain **untested**. Shared Minecraft-version labels are not evidence of interoperability.\n\n## Script-over-context decisions\n\n| Conflict | Production decision |\n|---|---|\n| Earlier material starts with Moss already present | Follow Scene 2: the protagonist arrives alone, survives, meets a wild wolf, tames it, later obtains a name tag by fishing and finally names it `MOSS`. |\n| Earlier material uses a surface portal hum | Follow Scenes 2–3: ordinary mining and exposed iron cause discovery; echo-portal audio begins only after the frame is visible underground. |\n| Earlier material repeats arrival at the ending | Follow Scene 13: repeat `MATCH FRAME A`, after Moss is tamed and named, as the pair begin the mining descent. |\n| Earlier material requires direct anchor discharge | Follow Scenes 11–12: the protagonist prepares but never ignites the frame; the falling creeper explodes first. |\n| Earlier material explains a fixed timeline and older builder | Exclude it. `draft-03` uses stable echo realities and one R4 source frame projecting the R0 receiving mouth. |\n| Earlier material resolves Moss’s fate | Exclude it. R4 Moss remains absent and unseen; show no body, collar drop, death message or locating sound. |\n\n## Provisional technical decision\n\nUse **Minecraft Java Edition 1.20.1 with Fabric** for the first isolated proof of concept.\n\nThis choice is based on the strongest supplied exact-release intersection:\n\n- Immersive Portals `5.2.0` for Fabric 1.20.1;\n- Multiworld `1.12`, listing Fabric 1.20.1;\n- Dimensional Weather `1.1-1.20.1`, with a stated Fabric API requirement of `0.92.2+1.20.1` or later;\n- Dimension Level Data `0.1.0-1.20.1` as an alternative independent time/weather candidate;\n- Carpet `1.4.112` for 1.20/1.20.1;\n- Axiom `5.2.1` for 1.20–1.20.1;\n- CinematicTools `1.2.0+1.20.1`, with Fabric API, GeckoLib and CreativeCore dependencies;\n- Replay Mod as a camera/replay candidate whose exact 1.20.1 artefact is still unpinned.\n\n### 1.20.1 versus 1.21.1\n\n| Capability | 1.20.1 evidence supplied | 1.21.1 evidence supplied | Decision |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| See-through portal | Immersive Portals 5.2.0 exact release | No exact release evidence | Test 1.20.1 first |\n| Separate echo worlds | Multiworld 1.12 exact release | No exact release evidence | Treat Multiworld integration as untested |\n| Independent weather | Dimensional Weather 1.1 exact release | No exact release evidence | Test one weather method at a time |\n| Independent time/state | Dimension Level Data 0.1.0 exact release | No exact release evidence | Add only if vanilla or weather control proves insufficient |\n| Deterministic scripting | Carpet 1.4.112 exact release | No exact release evidence | Datapack first, Carpet second |\n| World editing | Axiom 5.2.1 exact release | No exact release evidence | Use only after backup/reset proof |\n| Authored camera | CinematicTools 1.2.0 exact release; Replay exact build unresolved | No exact release evidence | Compare one camera tool at a time |\n| Performance, shaders and recording | No exact integrated versions supplied | No exact integrated versions supplied | Keep optional and test last |\n\nThe 1.21.1 route is not rejected on capability. It is deferred because the supplied evidence cannot establish an exact candidate intersection. Researching exact official 1.21.1 releases is a required paper gate before any migration test.\n\n### Candidate load order\n\n1. Minecraft Java 1.20.1, Java runtime, Fabric Loader and Fabric API, with exact versions still to be pinned.\n2. Immersive Portals only.\n3. One echo-world method: Multiworld first; a project datapack dimension design only if separately sourced and tested.\n4. One weather/time method: Dimensional Weather first; Dimension Level Data only for a proven gap.\n5. Project datapack `tpnm_take`.\n6. Carpet/Scarpet only where the datapack cannot produce repeatable timing or actor control.\n7. Either Replay Mod or CinematicTools first; add the other only for a documented missing capability.\n8. Axiom for build work and repair after backup procedures pass.\n9. Performance mods, shaders and recording integrations one at a time.\n\nFabric Loader, Fabric API, iCommon API, GeckoLib, CreativeCore, Replay Mod, recording software, Blender and shader/performance artefacts remain unpinned. Every addition requires a launch, save, reload and repeatability check. No combined compatibility is claimed.\n\n## Implementation architecture\n\n### World and geography layer\n\nCreate one untouched master location from one seed, one game version, one generator and one generation-affecting configuration. Derive R0–R4 from verified copies or controlled region duplication. The master must contain:\n\n- the ridge and `MATCH PATH` line;\n- the R0 overlook and `MATCH FRAME A` line;\n- the descent route;\n- the forked granite seam;\n- the exposed-iron turn;\n- the portal chamber and corresponding surface column.\n\nDo not use unrelated seeds. World IDs, seed, generator settings and copied regions may be recorded only after they exist.\n\n### Portal layer\n\nPreferred test path: Immersive Portals provides the live view and crossing while an independently registered world or dimension represents each echo. Exact destination commands and portal orientation must be recorded during the proof of concept.\n\nRequired topology:\n\n`R0 unkeyed entry → R1 → R2 → R3 → R4`\n\n`R4 completed source view → R0 cave`\n\n`R0 entry must still continue → R1`\n\nThis asymmetric condition is a blocker-level test. If it cannot coexist live, use shot-specific portal configurations or matched destination composites. The invented keying, creeper-triggered activation, particles and delayed portal response remain VFX/story canon, not claims about vanilla Minecraft or a mod.\n\n### Weather and time layer\n\nUse fixed time, disabled daylight cycling and disabled weather cycling for repeatable plates. Test dry R0 and rainy R1 simultaneously before adding shaders. The pass must show rain, destination light, waterfall and geometry through the portal from R0 and after crossing. If separate worlds do not retain independent time/weather, evaluate one documented candidate at a time.\n\n### Camera and capture layer\n\nLocked views use numerical transforms and planned local marks. Portal-parallax shots require lateral motion; match cuts use static or exactly repeated paths. Replay Mod and CinematicTools are alternatives until tested. Native or external recording software, codec, resolution and frame-rate remain unselected. A 24 fps editorial target may be used for path design, but no performance target is considered achieved.\n\n### Composite and Blender fallback\n\nWhere live rendering fails, record separately controlled source and destination plates with identical camera geometry. Composite the destination into a tracked portal mask, preserve foreground occlusion, add restrained tear particles and keep rain/audio on destination-specific layers. Scene 13 may use modular stone-and-soil plates and matched dissolves rather than a literal continuous underground flight. Blender is a candidate for greyboxing, camera matching and depth-assisted composites; its exact version, licence record and plug-ins must be verified before use.\n\n### Custom-development gate\n\nNo custom mod is recommended now. It becomes eligible only after:\n\n1. an existing-tool test has a reproducible failure;\n2. exact versions, logs, steps and expected versus actual behaviour are retained;\n3. the composite or shot-specific configuration fallback is judged inadequate;\n4. the missing behaviour is expressed as a narrow acceptance test; and\n5. the human approves the added scope and any BRL cost.\n\n## Scene synthesis\n\nDetailed controls are in the scene implementation and test matrices.\n\n| Scene | Preferred production route | Deterministic control | Camera/VFX route | Test gate |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | R4 night plate plus controlled smoke and dropped cargo | Fixed marks, time, weather and tagged cargo | Locked `MATCH PATH`; separate smoke if needed | CONT-001, VFX-003 |\n| 2 | State-based R0 montage with separately blocked hostile-mob and wolf plates | Wild, tamed-unnamed and named states; scripted skeleton release; controlled fishing insert | Locked arrival, short montage paths, `MATCH FRAME A` | MEC-001, MEC-002, MEC-003, CONT-001 |\n| 3 | Live portal discovery if proof passes | Fixed seam, iron turn, player and Moss threshold marks | Lateral parallax and threshold move; composite fallback | POC-003, MEC-003 |\n| 4 | R1 copy with fixed rain and marker state | Independent weather, one-block marker and journal state | Matched arrival and R1 surface plate | POC-004, CONT-002 |\n| 5 | Separate R2 and R3 states | Bare foot, L marker, block-count and journal inserts | Exact frame-foot close-ups | CONT-002, GFX-001 |\n| 6 | Compact archive set and controlled portal-failure plates | Atlas page order, gravel state and Moss exit mark | Locked inserts; contracted destination composite if required | GFX-001, VFX-001 |\n| 7 | Fresh R4 copy with staged mouth collapse | Incomplete-frame structure, failed ordinary-fire beat and surface marker | Matched arrival plus soft fade | POC-003, VFX-001 |\n| 8 | Milestone copies of the homestead | Rug states, Moss marks, fixed weather and build modules | Repeated locked montage compositions | MEC-003, MEC-004 |\n| 9 | Controlled Moss routine and separate fire-origin plate | Feed, sit, second gesture, isolated bark cue, fixed first fire block | Locked shared-room wide | AUD-001, MEC-004 |\n| 10 | Same R4 fire continuity window as Scene 1 where practical | Resettable doorway, water, falling timber, removable wall and search marks | Controlled fire/steam plates and burned-state hold | MEC-004, VFX-003, CONT-001 |\n| 11 | State-based final-frame construction in sacrificial chamber copy | Tagged creeper plant, exact ledge, frame states, anchor appearance and baffle marks | Brief first-person plant; locked construction fragments | MEC-005, MEC-006, CONT-003 |\n| 12 | Separate choice, fall, hiss, blast, aftermath and activation plates | Scripted creeper path, fixed cue ticks, protected aftermath state and curated items | Black-frame fatal cut and delayed composite activation | MEC-005, MEC-006, VFX-002 |\n| 13 | Omniscient frame approach, modular vertical transition and exact R0 repeat | Protected R0 established-pair state and one reused narration asset | Portal composite, stylised layers, `MATCH FRAME A` | CONT-001, EDIT-001, AUD-001 |\n\n## Resettable take controller\n\nCreate the project datapack namespace `tpnm_take` before complex rehearsals. Each take exposes five functions:\n\n1. `setup/<take_id>` restores the correct region or structure, sets game rules, establishes time/weather, removes only tagged temporary entities and creates marks.\n2. `arm/<take_id>` teleports performers to marks, freezes or holds them, resets objectives, places the camera and displays a ready cue.\n3. `action/<take_id>` starts a tick counter, releases only required actors and emits a synchronisation cue.\n4. `reset/<take_id>` clears tagged fire, items, projectiles and temporary actors, restores the source state and returns to `arm`.\n5. `cleanup/<take_id>` removes take-only marks, tags and objectives without touching persistent Moss, protected builds or the clean master.\n\nPlanned objectives are `tpnm_take`, `tpnm_phase`, `tpnm_tick` and `tpnm_cue`. All temporary entities receive both a broad `tpnm.temp` tag and a take-specific tag. Marker entities identify actor, camera, landing, prop and eyeline positions.\n\nGlobal take controls include fixed time/weather, `doDaylightCycle false`, `doWeatherCycle false`, `doMobSpawning false`, a recorded difficulty, and restoration of every changed game rule during cleanup. Syntax and dimension scope must be verified in the selected build.\n\nSafety rules:\n\n- A wild wolf, tamed unnamed wolf and named Moss are distinct continuity states. Do not silently substitute one persistent entity for another.\n- Ownership, collar, name, health and sit state must be inspected after save/reload and portal crossing.\n- Skeleton action is released from fixed marks; separate threat and intervention plates are preferred over natural targeting RNG.\n- Fishing remains the story cause, but the production insert must not depend on waiting for an uncontrolled random catch.\n- Fire uses a fixed ignition mark and backed-up room. Exact burn-fan continuity should use progressive state copies if spread is not repeatable.\n- The creeper follows a connected, visible ledge-to-landing route. Fall, hiss, blast and aftermath may be separate plates.\n- Dropped items are tagged or art-directed from test evidence, then checked to exclude Moss-related or continuity-breaking items.\n\nThe complete controller specification is in technical research. It is designed but not implemented or tested.\n\n## Continuity locks\n\n### MATCH PATH\n\nScenes 1, 2 and 10 use one planned camera transform, height, FOV, path centreline and travel direction. R0 morning and R4 fire-night are different set states around that invariant. Scenes 1 and 10 should be captured within one restorable R4 fire window when feasible.\n\n### MATCH FRAME A\n\nCreate only after Moss has helped against the skeleton, been tamed, received the name tag `MOSS` and joined established routines. Preserve camera, sun direction, weather, equipment, journal condition, pack action, protagonist mark, Moss mark and action timing. Record the line once and reuse the same audio in Scene 13:\n\n`Below the hill was only another day's work. They went together.`\n\n### Granite seam\n\nThe seam remains natural geography. Its fork, scale and screen position identify matching coordinates in all echoes. R0’s iron vein continues beyond it and causes the turn towards the portal.\n\n### Moss\n\nNo collar or name before its scripted beat. No R4 post-fire shot or sound may resolve Moss’s fate. The Scene 12 bark is the exact Scene 9 performance filtered as memory, not a bark located in the ravine.\n\n### Creeper route\n\nThe Scene 11 dark ledge must physically connect to the Scene 12 landing mark. The green edge is sub-second, peripheral and unstressed. The protagonist raises flint and steel but does not ignite the frame before the blast.\n\n## Storyboard and camera design\n\nThe text-first storyboard contains 49 planned panels, at least two for every scene, with extra coverage for portals, match frames, hostile-mob action, fire, the creeper route and Scene 13. Each ledger entry provides:\n\n- a literal frame and 3×3 grid;\n- a planned local camera position, height and FOV;\n- foreground, midground and background;\n- subject marks, facing and eyeline;\n- movement stated as directions in words;\n- lighting direction;\n- environment, audio and transition;\n- continuity anchor and capture purpose.\n\nLocal coordinates are design marks, not claims about an existing world. Actual Minecraft coordinates may be recorded only after the master location exists.\n\nNo storyboard image has been generated. For a later optional sketch pass, use actual Minecraft or Blender greybox screenshots as composition-locked references. The provisional first model test is ChatGPT Images 2.0, with FLUX.2 Pro as the multi-reference comparison and Midjourney as a style exploration reserve. Run only the defined five-panel consistency test before scaling.\n\n## Location and build strategy\n\nBuild only what appears in camera-safe directions. The master ravine, seam, portal chamber and surface column are reused; echo identity comes from replaceable water, vegetation, ash, archive, weather, sound and local history. R4 uses separately restorable milestones:\n\n- fresh arrival;\n- first roof;\n- growing home;\n- lived room with each rug stage;\n- pre-fire room;\n- burning doorway;\n- breached and burned room;\n- final-frame chamber;\n- protagonist-free aftermath.\n\nThe complete location plan, eleven cards and build budget define modules and cut lines. Do not build all five full worlds before the portal/weather proof produces either a live pass or an approved composite recipe.\n\n## Evidence-producing order\n\n1. Complete missing exact-version research, especially the 1.21.1 comparison and dependency pins.\n2. Run POC-001 with Minecraft 1.20.1, Fabric and Immersive Portals only.\n3. Add one world method and verify matching geography, destinations and reload.\n4. Add one weather/time method and prove dry R0 viewing rainy R1.\n5. Implement the smallest datapack controller and repeat one setup–action–reset cycle twice after reload.\n6. Test player and Moss crossing, then asymmetric R4→R0/R0→R1 routing.\n7. Compare Replay Mod and CinematicTools one at a time.\n8. Establish a no-shader performance baseline; add optional rendering tools last.\n9. Approve the master location and continuity marks; preserve the untouched source.\n10. Build and capture non-destructive R0 milestones before echo and R4 progression.\n11. Test fire and blast only in sacrificial copies.\n12. Build a text-and-greybox animatic before final narration and principal capture.\n\n## Capture and post-production policy\n\n- No capture filename, take, selected take or usability result exists.\n- Record actual filenames only after files exist, using the approved slug/scene/shot/setup/take/date convention.\n- Preserve exact world states and two independent backups where available before destructive work.\n- Inspect picture, sound, UI, entity states, portal geometry and forbidden Moss evidence before a take can be considered usable.\n- Live portals are conditional. Composite plates are an authored fallback, not a failed imitation.\n- No narration follows the protagonist’s death.\n- Keep conventional-portal, echo-portal, rain, fire, bark and synchronisation stems isolated.\n- Final narration changes may improve clarity but may not add a surface hum, change causes, resolve Moss or imply survival.\n\n## Budget and cut line\n\nNo cash spend is authorised. The planning budget records labour hours and `BRL 0 authorised` for every package until an exact quote or purchase receives human approval.\n\nThe minimum viable version retains all thirteen causal scenes, the skeleton-to-bones-to-taming chain, fishing-to-name-tag cause, both marker absences, Atlas evidence, R4 domestic life, rug growth, fire path, unresolved absence, connected creeper route, fatal interruption, delayed portal activation and `MATCH FRAME A` ending.\n\nCut in this order if capacity is exceeded:\n\n1. shaders and cosmetic rendering mods;\n2. generated sketch conversion after the text/greybox board;\n3. extra background dressing and wide echo coverage;\n4. redundant montage angles;\n5. a literal continuous Scene 13 ascent, replacing it with matched modular dissolves.\n\nDo not cut a causal scene, Moss-state transition, portal rule, match frame or creeper-route evidence.\n\n## Rights and business controls\n\nExact source, publisher, licence, version, artefact name and hash must be recorded before software or third-party media enters Production. No skin, font, sound, music, plug-in or external asset is approved by this plan. Original work requires an authorship record once created. No purchase, commission or external message is authorised. Any future cost must be quoted in BRL and approved before commitment.\n\n## Completion record\n\n| Item | Status | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| Production synthesis | Deepened proposal | This document and auxiliary planning registers |\n| 1.20.1 exact component candidates | Partly researched | Official/project sources in the supplied ledger; dependencies remain unpinned |\n| 1.21.1 exact intersection | Blocked by evidence gap | No exact 1.21.1 release evidence supplied |\n| Combined stack | Untested | No launch, log, save or reload evidence |\n| Take controller | Designed only | No datapack or run evidence |\n| Master world and locations | Not created | Cards and modules are plans |\n| Storyboard | Text-first plan complete | 49 planned ledger panels; no image generated |\n| Mechanics and VFX tests | Not run | Test matrix only |\n| Narration and bark | Not recorded | Reuse requirements only |\n| Captures | None recorded | Capture and audio-capture logs remain untouched |\n| Selected take | None | Human selection cannot occur without capture evidence |\n| Technical usability | Not assessed | No captured take exists |\n\nProduction remains open. The next evidence-producing action is the isolated 1.20.1 portal/world/weather proof of concept. Capture-log and selected-take checks must remain blocked until genuine captures exist and receive human review.","files":[{"path":".studio/internal/production/storyboard-plan.md","content":"# Storyboard plan\n\n> Text-first storyboard designed for a creator with aphantasia. No image has been generated, embedded or approved. The panel ledger contains 49 planned panels and is the literal frame authority.\n\n## Visual grammar\n\n### Frame and coordinates\n\n- Delivery frame: 16:9 landscape. Keep essential evidence inside the central 80% title-safe area.\n- Every panel uses a named local coordinate system. These are proposed blocking marks, not existing Minecraft coordinates.\n- `X` increases towards camera-right, `Y` increases upwards and `Z` increases away from the camera along the principal view axis unless a panel states otherwise.\n- A camera entry always gives its local position, height, facing direction and planned horizontal FOV. Actual in-game transforms must replace local marks only after the master set exists.\n- Environment descriptions explicitly separate foreground, midground and background.\n- The 3×3 grid is written as `TL/TM/TR`, `ML/MM/MR`, `BL/BM/BR` so no spatial inference is required.\n\n### Lens and height families\n\n- 35°–42° FOV: journal, Atlas, marker and material-ledger inserts.\n- 48°–55° FOV: human-scale performance, portal hero views and exact continuity frames.\n- 58°–68° FOV: environmental geography and action where route readability matters.\n- Normal protagonist-height camera: 1.6–1.8 blocks.\n- Raised observational camera: 2.2–3.2 blocks.\n- Low Moss or floor-detail camera: 0.6–1.0 blocks.\n- Omniscient Scene 13 camera is identified explicitly and never shares the protagonist’s head height or movement language after death.\n\n### Composition and movement\n\n- Screen direction remains consistent within an action. Movement is stated as words such as `left to right`, `towards upper centre` or `down and away`.\n- Portal views preserve the frame plane, destination horizon and parallax direction. A lateral camera move right must reveal more of the destination’s left occluded edge.\n- Granite-seam recognition uses silhouette and screen placement, not colour grade alone.\n- Matches use numerical camera marks and reference overlays once those references genuinely exist.\n- Fire, mobs and portal activation may be divided into plates. The storyboard describes the final edit, not an assertion that one continuous take is possible.\n\n### Local set diagrams\n\n`MATCH PATH`, looking towards the homestead:\n\n    BG: homestead / smoke at Z+18\n                  ↑ travel\n    ridge path ── H ─────────────\n                  ↑\n             cargo mark\n                  ↑\n    CAM MP-C at Z-10\n\nPortal chamber, plan view:\n\n    destination side Z+\n         granite seam and destination cave\n                    |\n              [ portal plane ]\n                    |\n    source side Z-     CAM moves X-left → X-right\n\nHomestead shared room, plan view:\n\n    timber wall and fire route →\n    [hearth] [green rug/Moss] [timber floor]\n          doorway ↓          shortest wall at camera-left\n              CAM HR-C\n\nFinal chamber, elevation:\n\n    dark ledge L ● ── falling route ↓\n                              landing ● behind H\n    frame [====]   H ●   stone baffle [###]\n    chamber floor ─────────────────────────\n\nScene 13 elevation:\n\n    R0 surface / MATCH FRAME A\n    soil module\n    stone module\n    forked granite seam\n    active R0 mouth\n       ↑ audience-only camera path\n    active R4 source frame\n\n## Consistency pack for later sketch generation\n\n### Fixed subjects\n\n- Protagonist: one silent Minecraft avatar. Early R0 kit is simpler and cleaner; later R4 kit carries the weathered journals and final materials. Do not invent facial acting unavailable to the skin.\n- Wild wolf: no collar and no name.\n- Tamed unnamed wolf: collar visible, no `Moss` label.\n- Named Moss: same wolf silhouette and collar, with the name visible only when required by the panel.\n- Never depict a second protagonist, an older-self conversation, a Moss body, collar drop or death message.\n\n### Fixed props and places\n\n- Clean survey journal: stitched corner, mostly blank pages, three-line ravine symbol and arrow-shaped seven.\n- Weeping Atlas: weathered version of the same journal with only the seven Script-approved inserts.\n- Portal: crying-obsidian frame, directional tear particles and a transparent destination view; ordinary Nether portal remains visually distinct.\n- Geography: forked lightning-shaped granite seam, same scale and placement in all echoes.\n- Hearth: stone-backed open fire; moss-green rug grows one square at a time.\n- Final chamber: completed frame, charged-anchor appearance, offset stone baffle and connected dark creeper ledge.\n\n### Restrained sketch aesthetic\n\nTransform a real Minecraft or Blender greybox reference into a practical storyboard drawing: graphite construction lines, sparse black-ink contour, one flat grey shadow value and a single muted purple annotation only where the portal plane must be identified. Preserve block geometry, camera angle and subject marks. Do not add cinematic fog, costume detail, dramatic anatomy, extra props, textural decoration or lighting not present in the reference.\n\nNegative constraints: no photorealism; no painterly fantasy portal; no extra characters; no wolf breed change; no curved non-Minecraft architecture; no altered frame asymmetry; no shifted granite seam; no readable text invented by the model; no body or remains; no post-death protagonist viewpoint.\n\n### Reference-first workflow\n\n1. Build or greybox the panel using the panel’s local marks.\n2. Capture the actual camera view after the relevant technical test passes.\n3. Supply that screenshot as the primary composition reference.\n4. Supply the approved protagonist, Moss, portal, journal and location references only when visible.\n5. Request transformation rather than independent scene invention.\n6. Compare the result with the source using an overlay and a written continuity checklist.\n7. Retain prompt, model identity, source provenance and human decision only after generation actually occurs.\n\n## Scene panels\n\nThe CSV ledger contains every required field. The descriptions below identify the intended reading order and spatial problem each panel solves.\n\n### Scene 1 — panels P01-01 to P01-02\n\n- P01-01: the protagonist crests the R4 ridge; smoke sits behind the path line and purple cargo is physically visible before it is dropped.\n- P01-02: locked `MATCH PATH`; the protagonist runs away from camera towards the homestead. The same motion line cuts to P02-01.\n\n### Scene 2 — panels P02-01 to P02-06\n\n- P02-01 repeats P01-02’s camera exactly in untouched morning R0, but the protagonist walks rather than runs and arrives alone.\n- P02-02 establishes the overlook, water, birches and the choice to stop.\n- P02-03 makes the skeleton-to-wild-wolf intervention readable without showing a collar.\n- P02-04 holds bones between protagonist and wolf; hearts and collar belong only after the offered-bones action.\n- P02-05 shows the anvil, `MOSS` name tag and application after the fishing cause.\n- P02-06 is `MATCH FRAME A`: named Moss beside the packed protagonist before both descend.\n\n### Scene 3 — panels P03-01 to P03-04\n\n- P03-01 puts the granite seam and exposed iron on one continuous route.\n- P03-02 reveals the crying frame only after the turn.\n- P03-03 is the lateral parallax proof: dry source foreground, rainy destination background.\n- P03-04 holds protagonist and Moss crossing together with audio changing at the plane.\n\nPortal blocking:\n\n    dry R0 source: H ●  M ●  →  [frame]  →  rain R1\n    camera track: X-2 ─────────────→ X+2\n\n### Scene 4 — panels P04-01 to P04-03\n\n- P04-01 completes the crossing beside the same seam and visible waterfall.\n- P04-02 frames the recognisable surface without shelter, crops or cow pen.\n- P04-03 shows the single cobblestone block against the left frame foot before entry into the dry view.\n\n### Scene 5 — panels P05-01 to P05-03\n\n- P05-01 exactly repeats the frame-foot insert with the R1 block absent.\n- P05-02 makes the R2 two-block L and outer torch unambiguous.\n- P05-03 repeats the bare foot in R3, then presents the coordinate/marker comparison and `ECHOES` consequence.\n\nMarker plan:\n\n    R1: [left frame foot][one cobble]\n    R2: [left frame foot][cobble]\n                         [cobble+torch]\n    R3: [left frame foot][bare floor]\n\n### Scene 6 — panels P06-01 to P06-04\n\n- P06-01 shows familiar torch and storage habits before the journal reveal.\n- P06-02 aligns the clean and weathered stitched corners.\n- P06-03 gives the seven Atlas instructions readable, separate holds rather than one overloaded frame.\n- P06-04 places blocked gravel behind the protagonist while the contracting portal remains the only open route.\n\n### Scene 7 — panels P07-01 to P07-02\n\n- P07-01 completes arrival in habitable R4 while projected upper blocks fade.\n- P07-02 shows ordinary fire failing at the incomplete mouth, then the surface marker and first roof as a causal sequence.\n\n### Scene 8 — panels P08-01 to P08-04\n\n- P08-01 repeats one exterior composition through build milestones.\n- P08-02 shows Moss occupying the exact block needed and the protagonist choosing to wait.\n- P08-03 repeats the same shared-room frame for bare floor, initial rug and final rug.\n- P08-04 links the desk ledger, conventional portal returns and measured dead mouth without implying haste.\n\n### Scene 9 — panels P09-01 to P09-03\n\n- P09-01 identifies the final two ledger entries.\n- P09-02 shows feed, return to rug, second sit gesture and the source bark performance.\n- P09-03 holds after departure until fire catches the nearest green square and travels out of frame towards timber.\n\n### Scene 10 — panels P10-01 to P10-05\n\n- P10-01 resumes the exact Scene 1 path movement.\n- P10-02 keeps the empty doorway, water stream, steam and falling timber in one readable axis.\n- P10-03 reveals the breached shortest wall, absent rug and charred fan without any Moss evidence.\n- P10-04 maps the search route from crops to ridge, ravine, portal shelter and covered hollow.\n- P10-05 shows dropped cargo, weathered Atlas, wolf figure and closing of the unfinished safety page.\n\n### Scene 11 — panels P11-01 to P11-04\n\n- P11-01 places the muted green edge at the extreme screen side and shows its connected dark ledge.\n- P11-02 matches the R4 frame’s asymmetry to the R0 mouth through labour stages.\n- P11-03 separates charged-anchor appearance from the keyed/unkeyed Atlas insert.\n- P11-04 makes baffle, reach, journals, protagonist and creeper landing route spatially legible.\n\nFinal chamber plan:\n\n    frame F at Z0\n          H ignition mark at Z-3\n    baffle B offset X-3, Z-4\n    camera C at X-6, Z-8\n    ledge L at X+1, Y+5, Z-4\n          ↓ connected fall\n    landing at X+1, Z-3.5 behind H\n\n### Scene 12 — panels P12-01 to P12-05\n\n- P12-01 holds the hand on the Atlas wolf figure while the reused bark is subjective.\n- P12-02 shows the raised flint and steel, landing position and creeper hiss before any ignition.\n- P12-03 is a literal black frame for the explosion sound and death interval.\n- P12-04 is a locked protagonist-free aftermath plate with restrained scattered items.\n- P12-05 stages flash, first particles and gradual R0 destination view in that order.\n\n### Scene 13 — panels P13-01 to P13-04\n\n- P13-01 begins outside the frame in the protagonist-free R4 aftermath.\n- P13-02 crosses into R0 and passes the granite seam as audience access.\n- P13-03 rises through modular stone and soil into `MATCH FRAME A`.\n- P13-04 repeats the exact Scene 2 image and narration, then cuts to the waiting R0 mouth showing R1 rain.\n\n## Review and generation gate\n\n### Text-board review\n\nA human reviewer should be able to answer, without imagining missing space:\n\n- where the camera is;\n- where every subject stands and faces;\n- which direction movement follows;\n- what is foreground, midground and background;\n- where light originates;\n- what changes at the cut;\n- which continuity anchor must match;\n- why the shot is being captured.\n\nAny ambiguous answer returns the panel to text revision before greyboxing.\n\n### Five-panel model consistency test\n\nUse actual greybox screenshots for these five cases:\n\n1. P02-05 — protagonist/Moss identity and readable prop relationship.\n2. P03-03 — portal-frame geometry, parallax and rainy destination preservation.\n3. P02-03 — hostile-mob action with three clear marks and no premature collar.\n4. P02-06 paired with P13-04 — exact match-frame preservation across two uses.\n5. P10-03 — fireplace, missing rug and burn-fan geometry without invented Moss evidence.\n\nFirst candidate: ChatGPT Images 2.0, based on the supplied official-source summary for instruction following, editing and continuity. Comparison candidate: FLUX.2 Pro for multi-reference editing and explicit composition/pose control. Midjourney’s Style and Omni Reference systems may be tested for aesthetic exploration but are not the first camera-faithful choice.\n\nApproval requires all five outputs to preserve aspect ratio, camera geometry, block layout, protagonist silhouette, Moss state, visible props, seam/frame asymmetry and the restrained graphite-and-ink language. Reject any model that invents story evidence or shifts essential marks. Permit at most two prompt revisions per failed panel before returning to the text/greybox board or comparing the alternative. No bulk generation follows without human approval.\n\nPanel IDs, not invented image filenames, identify this phase. If images are later generated, naming and provenance are recorded only after the files exist."},{"path":".studio/internal/research/source-ledger.csv","content":"source_id,claim,url,publisher,published_date,accessed_date,source_type,reliability,status,notes\n\"SRC-001\",\"In a single-past model, a time traveller cannot make the past different but may participate in the events that made it so.\",\"https://plato.stanford.edu/entries/time-travel/index.html\",\"Metaphysics Research Lab, Stanford University\",\"2024-03-22\",\"2026-07-15\",\"specialist_reference\",\"B\",\"retained_context\",\"Direction-era conceptual source; draft-03 instead uses stable echo realities. Not implementation evidence.\"\n\"SRC-002\",\"The proposed self-consistency principle requires local events in a closed-timelike-curve model to fit a globally consistent solution.\",\"https://authors.library.caltech.edu/records/aw0a8-ps286\",\"Physical Review D / American Physical Society\",\"1990-09-15\",\"2026-07-15\",\"primary_research\",\"A\",\"retained_context\",\"Conditional theoretical physics paper. It does not support the draft-03 echo mechanism or practical time travel.\"\n\"SRC-003\",\"Immersive Portals provides see-through seamless portals and portals connecting dimensions.\",\"https://modrinth.com/project/zJpHMkdD\",\"qouteall / Modrinth\",\"\",\"2026-07-16\",\"official_project_page\",\"A\",\"supported\",\"Apache-2.0 recorded in supplied research. Establishes individual capability only.\"\n\"SRC-004\",\"Immersive Portals documents a portal-destination command accepting dimension and exact position; connected portal entities can be removed for one-way configurations.\",\"https://qouteall.fun/immptl/wiki/Commands-Reference.html\",\"Immersive Portals official wiki\",\"\",\"2026-07-16\",\"official_documentation\",\"A\",\"supported\",\"Command syntax and behaviour still require verification against the exact selected release.\"\n\"SRC-005\",\"Multiworld documents creating worlds with generator and seed arguments and teleporting or routing portals to worlds and positions.\",\"https://github.com/IsaiahMC/multiworld\",\"IsaiahMC\",\"\",\"2026-07-16\",\"official_repository\",\"A\",\"supported\",\"LGPL-3.0 recorded in supplied research. Does not prove interoperability with Immersive Portals.\"\n\"SRC-006\",\"Multiworld 1.12 is a beta Fabric release listing Minecraft 1.20.1 compatibility.\",\"https://modrinth.com/mod/multiworld/version/NfNQTHy9\",\"Isaiah / Modrinth\",\"2025-12-21\",\"2026-07-16\",\"official_release_page\",\"A\",\"supported\",\"Documented individual version support only; iCommon API pin and integrated behaviour remain unresolved.\"\n\"SRC-007\",\"Dimensional Weather is intended to permit dimension-specific vanilla weather rather than sharing the Overworld weather state.\",\"https://modrinth.com/project/Z8Eq3K2Z\",\"crafter312 / Modrinth\",\"\",\"2026-07-16\",\"official_project_page\",\"A\",\"supported\",\"MIT recorded in supplied research. Portal-view rendering is outside this claim.\"\n\"SRC-008\",\"Dimensional Weather 1.1-1.20.1 lists Fabric/Quilt Minecraft 1.20.1 support and Fabric API 0.92.2+1.20.1 as a requirement.\",\"https://modrinth.com/mod/dimensional-weather/version/1.1-1.20.1\",\"crafter312 / Modrinth\",\"2024-06-20\",\"2026-07-16\",\"official_release_page\",\"A\",\"supported\",\"Exact Fabric API artefact must still be pinned; simultaneous use with other candidates is untested.\"\n\"SRC-009\",\"Minecraft Help describes copying a Java Edition seed to create a new world from the same base map.\",\"https://help.minecraft.net/hc/en-us/articles/34467817926925-How-to-Find-Your-World-Seed-in-a-Minecraft-Java-Edition-Realm\",\"Mojang Studios / Minecraft Help\",\"\",\"2026-07-16\",\"official_documentation\",\"A\",\"supported\",\"Same version, generator and generation-affecting configuration remain necessary production controls.\"\n\"SRC-010\",\"Mojang describes seeds as numbers used to generate a world reliably when reused.\",\"https://www.minecraft.net/es-es/article/speedrunning-minecraft\",\"Mojang Studios\",\"2018-02-17\",\"2026-07-16\",\"official_article\",\"A\",\"supported\",\"Used only for the common-base principle; exact shot continuity still requires a protected master copy.\"\n\"SRC-011\",\"Immersive Portals 5.2.0 is listed for Minecraft 1.20.1 Fabric and the release notes mention updated Sodium and Iris compatibility.\",\"https://www.curseforge.com/minecraft/mc-mods/immersive-portals-mod/files/7247098\",\"qouteall / CurseForge\",\"2025-11-21\",\"2026-07-16\",\"official_release_page\",\"A\",\"supported\",\"Apache-2.0 recorded. No exact Sodium or Iris versions are established and the production stack remains untested.\"\n\"SRC-012\",\"Immersive Portals 5.2.0 is an exact Fabric 1.20.1 candidate release.\",\"https://modrinth.com/mod/immersiveportals/version/5.2.0\",\"qouteall / Modrinth\",\"\",\"2026-07-17\",\"official_release_page\",\"A\",\"supported\",\"Central provisional portal candidate. Exact downloaded artefact and hash do not exist in evidence.\"\n\"SRC-013\",\"The Multiworld project page lists Minecraft 1.20.1 as active and describes multiple-world functionality.\",\"https://modrinth.com/project/fgvoNDL1\",\"Isaiah / Modrinth\",\"\",\"2026-07-17\",\"official_project_page\",\"A\",\"supported\",\"Use with SRC-005 and SRC-006. Registration as an Immersive Portals destination remains a proof-of-concept question.\"\n\"SRC-014\",\"Dimension Level Data 0.1.0-1.20.1 is a candidate for storing time and weather separately by dimension.\",\"https://modrinth.com/mod/dimension-level-data/version/c2yUFutK\",\"official project publisher shown on Modrinth\",\"\",\"2026-07-17\",\"official_release_page\",\"A\",\"supported_with_boundary\",\"Exact licence and dependencies were not supplied. Test as an alternative, not automatically alongside Dimensional Weather.\"\n\"SRC-015\",\"Replay Mod provides session replay and cinematic camera functionality.\",\"https://www.replaymod.com/\",\"Replay Mod project\",\"\",\"2026-07-17\",\"official_project_page\",\"A\",\"supported_with_boundary\",\"Exact Minecraft 1.20.1 build, licence and portal-stack intersection are not supplied.\"\n\"SRC-016\",\"Replay Mod maintains official user documentation for recording, replay and camera workflows.\",\"https://www.replaymod.com/docs/\",\"Replay Mod project\",\"\",\"2026-07-17\",\"official_documentation\",\"A\",\"supported_with_boundary\",\"Capability source only; no capture test or exact artefact is recorded.\"\n\"SRC-017\",\"CinematicTools 1.2.0+1.20.1 is a Minecraft 1.20.1 Fabric candidate whose release lists Fabric API, GeckoLib and CreativeCore dependencies.\",\"https://modrinth.com/mod/cinematictools/version/1.2.0%2B1.20.1\",\"CinematicTools publisher / Modrinth\",\"\",\"2026-07-17\",\"official_release_page\",\"A\",\"supported\",\"Exact dependency versions and licence were not supplied. Compare with Replay Mod rather than assuming both are required.\"\n\"SRC-018\",\"Carpet 1.4.112 lists Minecraft 1.20 and 1.20.1 Fabric support and supplies technical control and Scarpet scripting.\",\"https://modrinth.com/mod/carpet/version/1.4.112\",\"gnembon / Modrinth\",\"\",\"2026-07-17\",\"official_release_page\",\"A\",\"supported\",\"MIT recorded in supplied research. Specific actor and tick behaviours remain test tasks.\"\n\"SRC-019\",\"Axiom 5.2.1 lists Minecraft 1.20–1.20.1 Fabric support as a world-editing candidate.\",\"https://modrinth.com/mod/axiom/version/5.2.1\",\"Axiom project / Modrinth\",\"\",\"2026-07-17\",\"official_release_page\",\"A\",\"supported_with_boundary\",\"Licence was not supplied. It does not replace verified master-world backups.\"\n\"SRC-020\",\"The supplied official OpenAI release summary describes ChatGPT Images 2.0 as improving instruction following, editing, style handling and multi-scene continuity.\",\"https://openai.com/index/introducing-chatgpt-images-2-0/\",\"OpenAI\",\"\",\"2026-07-17\",\"official_product_announcement\",\"A\",\"supported_with_boundary\",\"Basis for a later five-panel comparison only. No image was generated and no geometry-preservation test was run.\"\n\"SRC-021\",\"FLUX.2 official documentation describes multi-reference image editing and controls for composition and pose.\",\"https://docs.bfl.ai/flux_2/flux2_image_editing\",\"Black Forest Labs\",\"\",\"2026-07-17\",\"official_documentation\",\"A\",\"supported_with_boundary\",\"Comparison candidate for reference-heavy storyboard transformation; no project test has occurred.\"\n\"SRC-022\",\"Midjourney documents Omni Reference for maintaining referenced subjects or objects.\",\"https://docs.midjourney.com/hc/en-us/articles/36285124473997-Omni-Reference\",\"Midjourney\",\"\",\"2026-07-17\",\"official_documentation\",\"A\",\"supported_with_boundary\",\"Useful comparison evidence, not proof of camera-faithful storyboard conversion.\"\n\"SRC-023\",\"Midjourney documents Style Reference for carrying visual style between generations.\",\"https://docs.midjourney.com/hc/en-us/articles/32180011136653-Style-Reference\",\"Midjourney\",\"\",\"2026-07-17\",\"official_documentation\",\"A\",\"supported_with_boundary\",\"Style control does not by itself establish composition or location consistency.\"\n\"SRC-024\",\"No exact Minecraft 1.21.1 release intersection for the portal, world, weather, actor, editor and camera candidates is present in the supplied source set.\",\"\",\"Production evidence review\",\"2026-07-17\",\"2026-07-17\",\"evidence_gap_record\",\"A\",\"unresolved\",\"This is a record of missing evidence, not a claim that compatible 1.21.1 releases do not exist. Exact official release pages must be researched before comparison.\"\n\"SRC-025\",\"No supplied source pins an exact Fabric Loader, complete Fabric API, iCommon API, GeckoLib or CreativeCore dependency chain for the proposed integrated profile.\",\"\",\"Production evidence review\",\"2026-07-17\",\"2026-07-17\",\"evidence_gap_record\",\"A\",\"unresolved\",\"Do not install by inference. Resolve exact dependency metadata and record artefact hashes during the isolated proof.\"\n\"SRC-026\",\"No supplied primary-source record establishes exact OBS or other recording software, Blender, Sodium, Iris, codec or driver versions for this production.\",\"\",\"Production evidence review\",\"2026-07-17\",\"2026-07-17\",\"evidence_gap_record\",\"A\",\"unresolved\",\"These remain selectable test categories rather than researched exact components.\""},{"path":".studio/internal/research/claims.md","content":"# Claims and evidence map\n\nUse this map for technical facts, licences, business decisions and explicit evidence gaps. Draft-03 story canon is separated from real-world claims.\n\n## Supported production claims\n\n### C-P01 — See-through portals and exact destinations are documented capabilities\n\n**Claim:** Immersive Portals documents seamless see-through portal travel and a command-level method for assigning a destination dimension and position.\n\n**Support:** SRC-003, SRC-004 and SRC-012.\n\n**Use:** Justifies an isolated live-portal proof before defaulting to compositing or custom development.\n\n**Boundary:** It does not prove Multiworld interoperability, asymmetric routing, destination weather, wolf transfer, replay visibility, shader compatibility or stable capture.\n\n### C-P02 — A 1.20.1 multiple-world candidate exists\n\n**Claim:** Multiworld documents multiple-world creation and an exact Fabric release `1.12` listing Minecraft 1.20.1.\n\n**Support:** SRC-005, SRC-006 and SRC-013.\n\n**Use:** Candidate representation for R0–R4 as separate saved world states.\n\n**Boundary:** Individual release support is not proof that Immersive Portals can resolve those worlds as dimensions or preserve portal state after reload.\n\n### C-P03 — Independent weather/time candidates exist for 1.20.1\n\n**Claim:** Dimensional Weather `1.1-1.20.1` is intended to separate vanilla weather by dimension, while Dimension Level Data `0.1.0-1.20.1` is described as separating dimension-level time and weather data.\n\n**Support:** SRC-007, SRC-008 and SRC-014.\n\n**Use:** Candidate methods for dry R0 viewing rainy R1 and for independently fixed echo lighting.\n\n**Boundary:** They are alternatives until tested. Their coexistence, world-method integration, portal-view rendering and audio behaviour are not supported claims.\n\n### C-P04 — One seed and one generation configuration are the correct starting principle\n\n**Claim:** Mojang documentation supports reusing a seed to create the same base world.\n\n**Support:** SRC-009 and SRC-010.\n\n**Use:** R0–R4 begin from one master geography so the ravine, granite seam, cave and surface align.\n\n**Boundary:** A seed alone is insufficient if game version, generator, datapacks or generation-affecting mods differ. Exact continuity therefore uses an untouched master and verified copies.\n\n### C-P05 — Carpet is an existing programmable control candidate\n\n**Claim:** Carpet `1.4.112` lists Fabric support for Minecraft 1.20/1.20.1 and includes technical control with Scarpet scripting.\n\n**Support:** SRC-018.\n\n**Use:** Second control layer after vanilla commands and the project datapack.\n\n**Boundary:** No exact actor sequence, fake-player route, tick behaviour or compatibility with the proposed stack has been tested.\n\n### C-P06 — Axiom is an existing 1.20.1 world-editing candidate\n\n**Claim:** Axiom `5.2.1` lists Fabric support for Minecraft 1.20–1.20.1.\n\n**Support:** SRC-019.\n\n**Use:** Candidate for build variants and manual region repair after the master backup procedure is proven.\n\n**Boundary:** It is not the sole reset or backup system. Exact licence, artefact and stack stability are unresolved.\n\n### C-P07 — Two camera routes have documented individual capability\n\n**Claim:** Replay Mod provides replay/cinematic-camera workflows, and CinematicTools has an exact `1.2.0+1.20.1` candidate release.\n\n**Support:** SRC-015, SRC-016 and SRC-017.\n\n**Use:** Compare one at a time for numerical paths, entity visibility and portal capture.\n\n**Boundary:** Replay Mod’s exact 1.20.1 artefact is unpinned. CinematicTools’ dependency pins are unresolved. Neither combined behaviour has been tested.\n\n### C-P08 — The exact 1.20.1 evidence intersection is stronger than the supplied 1.21.1 evidence\n\n**Claim:** The supplied sources contain exact 1.20.1 candidates for the central portal, world, weather, scripting, editing and one camera path, but contain no exact 1.21.1 candidate intersection.\n\n**Support:** SRC-006, SRC-008, SRC-012, SRC-014 and SRC-017 through SRC-019; missing-evidence record SRC-024.\n\n**Use:** Select 1.20.1 as the first proof-of-concept baseline.\n\n**Boundary:** This is an evidence-completeness decision. It is not a claim that 1.21.1 is less capable, unsupported or incompatible.\n\n### C-P09 — A reference-first image-editing comparison is justified\n\n**Claim:** The supplied official summaries support testing ChatGPT Images 2.0 for instruction-following and edits, FLUX.2 Pro for multi-reference editing and Midjourney for reference/style systems.\n\n**Support:** SRC-020 through SRC-023.\n\n**Use:** Run a five-panel screenshot-to-graphite-board comparison after real greyboxes exist.\n\n**Boundary:** No project image has been generated. Model consistency, exact composition preservation, terms and production suitability remain unverified.\n\n## Provisional engineering inferences\n\n### C-I01 — Existing tools should be tested before custom development\n\nImmersive Portals, a separate-world method, a weather/time method, vanilla commands, a project datapack and Carpet collectively make an existing-tool proof reasonable.\n\nThis is an inference from separate capabilities, not evidence that the stack works together. A custom mod remains deferred until a retained test isolates a specific unmet requirement.\n\n### C-I02 — Live and composite portal routes should be designed in parallel\n\nThe live route promises correct parallax and continuous crossing, while matched plates provide a controlled fallback for weather, topology, replay and performance failures. Designing both does not assert either has passed.\n\n### C-I03 — Progressive fire and aftermath states are safer than relying on RNG\n\nThe Script needs a legible rug-to-timber burn fan and reproducible continuity, not a documentary record of uncontrolled fire spread. If the exact mechanism is not repeatable, state-based plates preserve the scripted cause without claiming a continuous simulation.\n\n## Unresolved technical claims\n\nThe following must not be written as facts or successful results:\n\n- the complete 1.20.1 stack launches or reloads;\n- exact Fabric Loader/API and dependency pins are compatible;\n- Multiworld worlds are directly usable as Immersive Portals destinations;\n- the R4→R0 view can coexist with R0→R1 entry;\n- R1 rain, light and particles render correctly through an R0 portal;\n- a named tamed wolf crosses while retaining owner, name, collar, pose and health;\n- Replay Mod or CinematicTools records the portal and all entities correctly;\n- Sodium, Iris, shaders or capture software operate with acceptable performance;\n- vanilla fire creates the required rug-to-timber fan repeatably;\n- the planned skeleton/wolf action, fishing insert or creeper route is repeatable;\n- a creeper blast leaves the required frame and baffle geometry;\n- an anchor flashes or an echo frame activates because of that blast;\n- the Scene 13 transition reads as omniscient rather than post-death consciousness;\n- any exact 1.21.1 intersection exists or fails to exist;\n- any storyboard model preserves the project’s character and location consistency.\n\n## Draft-03 story canon, not technical claims\n\n- R0–R4 are stable echo realities with corresponding geography and incompatible histories.\n- An unkeyed crying-frame entry advances to the next mouth.\n- The completed R4 source frame projects the R0 receiving mouth.\n- Builder presence at ignition keys a route to `FIRST THRESHOLD`.\n- The protagonist prepares the frame but a falling creeper explodes before he ignites it.\n- The explosion kills the protagonist.\n- The charged anchor gives a later violet flash and the portal activates too late.\n- The Scene 13 camera is omniscient audience presentation.\n- R4 Moss’s fate remains unresolved.\n\nThese are fictional rules or scripted events. Crying-frame travel, keying, creeper-triggered activation and the delayed frame response must never be presented as vanilla Minecraft behaviour or verified mod behaviour.\n\n## Superseded context excluded from Production\n\n- one fixed timeline;\n- an older version of the protagonist constructing the opening portal;\n- direct anchor discharge by the protagonist;\n- a surviving protagonist rescuing Moss after the fire;\n- a final image of the pair walking away from a burned home.\n\nThose ideas remain historical development context and cannot override `draft-03`.\n\n## Evidence gaps and contradictions\n\n- The exact 1.20.1 central releases are documented individually, but there is no integrated proof. This is not a source contradiction; it is missing interoperability evidence.\n- The supplied source set contains no exact 1.21.1 releases. The comparison therefore records an unresolved evidence gap rather than inventing a candidate stack.\n- Immersive Portals release notes mention Sodium/Iris compatibility without supplying exact production pins. Those tools remain optional and last in the test order.\n- Dimensional Weather and Dimension Level Data overlap. Add one at a time and retain the simpler passing method.\n- Replay Mod and CinematicTools overlap. Compare them against panel and capture requirements rather than installing both by default.\n- Exact recording, Blender, shader, codec, driver and operating-environment evidence is absent.\n\n## Promotion rule\n\nA claim may move from planned or provisional to verified only when the build log records the exact version, source, artefact name and hash; the test matrix procedure is executed; logs and visual evidence are retained; save/reload is repeated where relevant; and a human reviews the acceptance criteria. No supplied evidence meets that threshold yet."},{"path":".studio/internal/production/technical-research.md","content":"# Production technical research — The Portal That Nobody Made\n\n> Evidence snapshot supplied through 17 July 2026. This document separates official-source findings, recommendations, planned tests and verified results. No stack, build, capture or storyboard image has been created or tested.\n\n## Decision\n\nTest **Minecraft Java 1.20.1 + Fabric** first. It has the strongest exact-version evidence intersection in the supplied source set. This is a provisional baseline, not a technical lock.\n\nThe 1.21.1 comparison cannot honestly name a strongest exact stack because no exact 1.21.1 portal, world, weather, scripting, editor or camera releases were supplied. Record that as research task VER-121 rather than borrowing versions from memory or inferring support from project pages.\n\n## Exact-version comparison\n\n| Function | Minecraft 1.20.1 candidate | Dependency evidence | Minecraft 1.21.1 candidate | Evidence status |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Game | Java Edition 1.20.1 | Java runtime unpinned | Java Edition 1.21.1 | Both game versions are comparison targets; exact runtime evidence absent |\n| Loader | Fabric Loader, exact release unpinned | Fabric API pin unresolved | Fabric Loader, no exact release supplied | Evidence gap |\n| Portal render/routing | Immersive Portals 5.2.0 | Exact library chain not supplied | No exact release supplied | 1.20.1 individual support documented |\n| Multiple worlds | Multiworld 1.12 beta | iCommon API exact pin unresolved | No exact release supplied | 1.20.1 individual support documented |\n| Weather | Dimensional Weather 1.1-1.20.1 | Fabric API 0.92.2+1.20.1 or later stated | No exact release supplied | 1.20.1 individual support documented |\n| Time/weather alternative | Dimension Level Data 0.1.0-1.20.1 | Licence/dependencies not supplied | No exact release supplied | 1.20.1 individual support documented |\n| Take scripting | Carpet 1.4.112 | Fabric environment | No exact release supplied | 1.20.1 individual support documented |\n| World editing | Axiom 5.2.1 | Exact licence/dependencies not supplied | No exact release supplied | 1.20.1 individual support documented |\n| Authored camera | CinematicTools 1.2.0+1.20.1 | Fabric API, GeckoLib and CreativeCore; exact pins absent | No exact release supplied | 1.20.1 individual support documented |\n| Replay camera | Replay Mod, exact build unpinned | Exact Fabric/API intersection absent | No exact release supplied | Capability documented; versions unresolved |\n| Performance/shaders | Sodium/Iris mentioned by an Immersive Portals release note | Exact versions absent | No exact releases supplied | Optional research gap |\n| Recording | Tool and exact release unselected | Codec, resolution, driver and storage unselected | Tool and exact release unselected | Research gap |\n| Blender/compositing | Blender candidate, exact release unselected | Plug-ins and licence record not supplied | Same | Workflow recommendation only |\n\n### Why 1.20.1 wins the first test\n\nThe Script’s critical path is see-through portal geometry, distinct echo states, independent weather, repeatable performances, resets and camera matching. The supplied evidence names exact 1.20.1 candidates for most of those categories. It names no equivalent 1.21.1 intersection. Choosing 1.20.1 therefore reduces paper uncertainty; it does not establish runtime stability.\n\n### Migration condition\n\nResearch and test 1.21.1 only if:\n\n- a required 1.20.1 capability has no viable implementation;\n- an integrated 1.20.1 failure is reproducible and version-specific;\n- an exact 1.21.1 intersection is documented from official release pages; or\n- security, launcher or operating constraints make 1.20.1 impractical.\n\n## Candidate dependency chain\n\n| Component | Exact candidate | Known dependency evidence | Unresolved item |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Fabric profile | Minecraft 1.20.1 | Fabric environment required by candidates | Java, Loader and final API versions |\n| Immersive Portals | 5.2.0 | Fabric 1.20.1 release | Exact artefact, hash and libraries |\n| Multiworld | 1.12 | Fabric 1.20.1; iCommon API referenced in supplied assets | Exact iCommon release and destination interoperability |\n| Dimensional Weather | 1.1-1.20.1 | Fabric API 0.92.2+1.20.1 or later | Final API pin and interaction with world method |\n| Dimension Level Data | 0.1.0-1.20.1 | Separate dimension-level state described | Licence, dependencies and need after weather test |\n| Carpet | 1.4.112 | Fabric 1.20/1.20.1 | Exact interaction with portal and replay tools |\n| CinematicTools | 1.2.0+1.20.1 | Fabric API, GeckoLib, CreativeCore | Exact dependency releases and overlap with Replay Mod |\n| Replay Mod | Unpinned 1.20.1 candidate | Official replay/camera capability | Exact artefact and Fabric/API/Sodium/Iris intersection |\n| Axiom | 5.2.1 | Fabric 1.20–1.20.1 | Licence, exact artefact and stack impact |\n\n## Implementation options\n\n### Option A — live portals between registered echo worlds\n\nUse Immersive Portals for the destination view and crossing, with Multiworld or another separately documented world/dimension method for R0–R4. This best supplies live parallax and a continuous wolf crossing.\n\nUnknowns: destination registration, independent weather, one-way state, asymmetric route, entity transfer, reload persistence, camera recording and performance.\n\nDecision: first proof route, still untested.\n\n### Option B — live portal shell with shot-specific routing\n\nUse separate portal configurations for each shot or entry direction. The R4 source view can target R0 while the R0 entry configuration is restored to R1 for its own capture window.\n\nAdvantage: avoids requiring the complete asymmetric topology to exist simultaneously.\n\nCost: no single continuous world state demonstrates the topology; continuity must be carefully documented.\n\nDecision: permitted fallback if POC-005 fails.\n\n### Option C — composited destination plates\n\nCapture source and destination with the same camera transform. Track or lock the frame mask, include foreground portal-block occlusion, use a destination depth or matte layer, and add rain/particles/audio separately. Conceal character transfer with threshold occlusion or a controlled cut.\n\nAdvantage: deterministic weather, performance and camera control.\n\nCost: parallax requires a matching camera path and may need a 3D portal card or Blender projection.\n\nDecision: fully designed fallback, not tested.\n\n### Option D — custom mod\n\nDo not begin. A custom mod is justified only by a narrow failed acceptance test after Options A–C and existing actor tools have been evaluated.\n\n## Portal tests\n\nThe minimum live test uses only R0 and R1:\n\n1. Create separately identified same-base worlds from a clean master candidate.\n2. Verify cave, seam and surface coordinates.\n3. Create one temporary portal with source and destination transforms recorded.\n4. Capture a static view and a four-block lateral move.\n5. Cross with the player.\n6. Cross with a tamed named wolf and inspect state.\n7. Set R0 dry and R1 rainy; check particles, light, waterfall and audio from both sides.\n8. Save, exit and reload.\n9. Repeat steps 4–7.\n10. Preserve logs and exact artefact records.\n\nDo not dress R2–R4 until this produces either a live pass or a documented composite recipe.\n\n## Independent time and weather\n\nVanilla commands remain the first control for a single active state: set time, disable daylight cycling, set weather and disable weather cycling. Whether those values are independently stored across the chosen echo implementation is a test question.\n\nTest Dimensional Weather alone after the portal/world baseline. If weather separation succeeds but time remains shared, test Dimension Level Data alone in a copied profile. Do not retain both merely because their descriptions are complementary.\n\nAcceptance requires source and destination states to persist through save/reload and remain correct while viewed through the portal. Audio may be replaced in post even if visual weather passes.\n\n## Deterministic take-controller specification\n\n### Namespace and state\n\nUse datapack namespace `tpnm_take`. Proposed objectives:\n\n- `tpnm_take`: numeric take identifier;\n- `tpnm_phase`: 0 idle, 1 setup, 2 armed, 3 action, 4 reset;\n- `tpnm_tick`: action-relative tick;\n- `tpnm_cue`: synchronisation cue number.\n\nUse namespaced storage for non-score state only after syntax is verified. Every temporary entity receives `tpnm.temp` and a take-specific tag. Persistent story entities receive continuity tags but are never removed by broad cleanup selectors.\n\nMarker entities define:\n\n- `tpnm.mark.camera`;\n- `tpnm.mark.hero`;\n- `tpnm.mark.wolf`;\n- `tpnm.mark.skeleton`;\n- `tpnm.mark.creeper_ledge`;\n- `tpnm.mark.creeper_land`;\n- `tpnm.mark.eyeline`;\n- prop and item positions.\n\n### Function lifecycle\n\n#### `setup/<take_id>`\n\n- Confirm the active world-state ID through a human-readable title or actionbar.\n- Set recorded difficulty, time and weather.\n- Disable daylight/weather cycles and natural mob spawning.\n- Clear only entities tagged for this take.\n- Restore the set from a verified structure/region copy or switch to the correct world milestone.\n- Clear take-specific fire, projectiles and dropped items.\n- Create or validate markers.\n- Summon temporary actors with persistence and AI held, or validate the persistent Moss continuity state.\n- Set the phase to setup and tick to zero.\n\n#### `arm/<take_id>`\n\n- Teleport the player/camera and actors to their marks.\n- Apply the required facing and eyeline.\n- Set sit, health, name visibility and equipment states.\n- Hold actors through `NoAI`, barriers, sit state or a Scarpet controller, depending on the validated method.\n- Preload required chunks if the selected tools support a documented method.\n- Display `ARMED <take_id>` and emit a guide-only synchronisation cue.\n- Set phase to armed.\n\n#### `action/<take_id>`\n\n- Set phase to action and tick to zero.\n- Increment `tpnm_tick` from a central tick function.\n- Release only scheduled actors at named ticks.\n- Change structures, fire blocks, portal effects or audio guide cues only through the take function.\n- Record a visible or audible guide cue that can be removed in the final edit.\n\n#### `reset/<take_id>`\n\n- Stop scheduled actions.\n- Remove only take-tagged temporary actors, items, projectiles and fire.\n- Restore the known source structure or reload/switch to the protected milestone for destructive scenes.\n- Revalidate persistent Moss rather than recreating it silently.\n- Reset scores and call `arm/<take_id>` only after the restored state passes a quick identity check.\n\n#### `cleanup/<take_id>`\n\n- Remove take-only tags and marker entities.\n- Restore every game rule changed by setup.\n- Remove guide cues and temporary objectives only when no other take needs them.\n- Never delete the clean master, persistent Moss, journals, protected set states or untagged entities.\n\n### Entity handling\n\n#### Wild wolf\n\nUse a dedicated Scene 2 state with no collar, name or owner. Arm at a fixed mark. Release on a scheduled cue or capture its intervention separately. Natural target selection is not an acceptance criterion.\n\n#### Tamed unnamed wolf\n\nCreate this state through a rehearsed taming transition or a verified snapshot. The collar may appear; `Moss` must not. Owner data must be inspected after reload. Do not assume direct NBT editing preserves valid ownership.\n\n#### Named Moss\n\nApply the name tag visibly in the story beat, then protect the named continuity state. Log owner, collar colour, name, health, sit/follow state and coordinates during real tests. Portal transfer and save/reload each require inspection.\n\n#### Skeleton\n\nUse a take-tagged skeleton at a fixed mark with controlled equipment, health and release tick. Separate skeleton threat, wolf response and taming plates if paths are inconsistent. Remove arrows/projectiles on reset.\n\n#### Creeper\n\nUse one take-tagged creeper and connected ledge/landing marks. Test a genuine fall separately. For deterministic editorial plates, Scarpet or tick-based waypoint motion may control the visible descent, followed by a separately cued hiss. Do not claim that scripted motion is natural AI. Blast tests occur only in a sacrificial chamber copy.\n\n#### Fire\n\nKeep `doFireTick` disabled during setup and arm. Restore the pre-fire room, place the initial fire at the defined rug edge on the action cue and enable spread only for mechanics tests. Because spread can vary, the preferred production result is a set of progressive states that preserve the tested causal origin and final burn fan. Reset by restoring the region, not by trying to reverse individual random changes.\n\n#### Dropped items\n\nClear only take-tagged items during setup. For aftermath plates, place a restrained approved set at fixed marks after studying any real blast test. Exclude name tags, collars, wolf food arrangements or any item that could resolve Moss’s fate. Record natural scatter only as reference until reviewed.\n\n### Spawn suppression and safety\n\n- Disable natural mob spawning throughout controlled takes.\n- Keep working routes lit and barriers outside camera where practical.\n- Use a sacrificial copy for fire, wall breaking, explosions and portal-state experiments.\n- Never run destructive reset functions against the clean master.\n- Include a dry-run mode that displays target region and take ID without changing blocks.\n- Make cleanup selectors require both namespace and take tags.\n\n### Synchronisation\n\nUse a visible actionbar count and a guide-only sound or particle cue at tick zero. Record portal, bark, creeper hiss, explosion and narration as isolated stems. The Scene 9 bark source is reused exactly in Scene 12; it is not regenerated or re-performed.\n\n### Controller escalation order\n\n1. Vanilla commands, functions, tags, marker entities, scoreboards and structure/region restoration.\n2. Carpet/Scarpet for tick timing or actor motion a documented vanilla test cannot hold.\n3. CinematicTools or another sourced actor tool for a precise failed performance requirement.\n4. Composite plates and hidden cuts.\n5. Custom mod only after all preceding routes produce documented inadequacy.\n\n## World editing and reset\n\n- Protect one clean master and separate milestone copies.\n- Use structure templates for bounded non-entity modules where their size and block-entity behaviour are validated.\n- Use world/region copies for destructive homestead and final-chamber states.\n- Use Axiom as a manual editor and repair aid, never as the only recovery method.\n- Keep portal entities, persistent wolves and world-level weather outside assumptions about structure restoration until tested.\n- Before any reset, display world ID, region ID and source milestone for human confirmation.\n\n## Camera and replay comparison\n\n### Replay Mod\n\nStrength: recorded performance can be viewed through a later cinematic camera path.\n\nUnknowns: exact 1.20.1 artefact, portal interior rendering, cross-world entity recording, wolf state, weather, audio, Fabric API and performance-mod intersection.\n\n### CinematicTools 1.2.0+1.20.1\n\nStrength: exact 1.20.1 candidate and authored camera/actor purpose.\n\nUnknowns: exact dependencies, licence, portal rendering, save/reload stability and whether it solves requirements beyond Replay Mod.\n\n### Vanilla/spectator and locked transforms\n\nStrength: minimum dependency path for static plates and simple tracks.\n\nUnknowns: path interpolation and repeatable first-person action.\n\nDecision: prove static and lateral portal plates before adding a camera mod. Test Replay Mod and CinematicTools in separate copied profiles and retain the one with fewer unresolved requirements.\n\n## Performance, shaders and recording\n\nEstablish a no-shader baseline first. Record portal recursion settings, render distance, simulation distance, destination chunk state, resolution, frame-rate target, encoder, GPU, driver and frame-time evidence only when selected.\n\nAdd Sodium or Iris only from exact official releases compatible with the pinned profile. The supplied Immersive Portals note mentions compatibility but supplies no exact versions. Shaders are optional and first on the scope cut line.\n\nRecording software and codec are unselected. A candidate such as OBS or a tool-integrated renderer requires official-source, exact-version and licence review before use. Acceptance is a playable file with stable frame pacing, correct portal rendering and synchronisation—not a nominal frame-rate setting.\n\n## Blender and compositing fallback\n\nBlender is a provisional category for:\n\n- recreating the numerical camera and portal plane;\n- projecting destination footage onto a card or simple depth shell;\n- creating foreground occlusion masks;\n- greyboxing the Scene 13 vertical route;\n- transforming modular stone/soil plates through matched dissolves.\n\nNo exact Blender version, plug-in or successful workflow is claimed. If selected, record the official release, licence, colour-management settings, frame rate and render pipeline. A conventional editor/compositor may perform the same tasks if it preserves geometry more efficiently.\n\n## Storyboard image-model comparison\n\n| Candidate | Supplied official evidence | Composition preservation | Multi-reference support | Character/location consistency | Decision |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| ChatGPT Images 2.0 | Instruction following, editing, style handling and multi-scene continuity described | Promising but untested on project greyboxes | Supplied summary supports edits; exact project limit untested | Promising but unverified | First five-panel test |\n| FLUX.2 Pro | Multi-reference editing and explicit composition/pose controls documented | Strong test candidate | Explicitly documented | Must be measured across five panels | Comparison candidate |\n| Midjourney | Omni Reference and Style Reference documented | No supplied proof of exact camera preservation | Reference systems documented | Useful for subject/style exploration | Reserve, not first camera-faithful choice |\n\nThe workflow must transform actual Minecraft or Blender greyboxes, not invent independent scenes. The five panels test relationship, portal parallax, action, exact match and burned-room continuity. No image generation occurs in this phase.\n\n## Test order\n\n1. VER-120 dependency paper resolution.\n2. POC-001 clean launch.\n3. POC-002 world/geography and reload.\n4. POC-003 portal view, parallax and player crossing.\n5. POC-004 independent weather/time.\n6. POC-005 asymmetric topology.\n7. ACT-001 datapack lifecycle.\n8. MEC-003 Moss crossing/state.\n9. CAM-001 camera candidates.\n10. PERF-001 no-shader baseline, then optional rendering tools.\n11. Composite, fire, creeper, aftermath and Scene 13 tests.\n\n## Verified results\n\nNone. All technical statuses remain `not_run`, `research_candidate`, `evidence_gap` or `planned`."},{"path":".studio/internal/production/toolchain-matrix.csv","content":"component_id,category,candidate,exact_version,minecraft_version,loader,purpose,official_source,licence,compatibility_status,decision,fallback,notes\n\"TC-001\",\"game\",\"Minecraft Java Edition\",\"1.20.1\",\"1.20.1\",\"not applicable\",\"Common production baseline\",\"https://www.minecraft.net/\",\"Proprietary\",\"version target only; runtime untested\",\"provisional_baseline\",\"Compare 1.21.1 only after exact intersection research\",\"No installed game or Java runtime evidence supplied.\"\n\"TC-002\",\"loader\",\"Fabric Loader\",\"not pinned\",\"1.20.1\",\"Fabric\",\"Load candidate mods\",\"https://fabricmc.net/\",\"Apache-2.0 recorded in supplied assets\",\"exact release and integrated chain unresolved\",\"required_research\",\"Pin from official dependency metadata\",\"Do not select by newest-version inference.\"\n\"TC-003\",\"api\",\"Fabric API\",\"minimum 0.92.2+1.20.1 stated by Dimensional Weather; final pin absent\",\"1.20.1\",\"Fabric\",\"Shared mod API\",\"https://modrinth.com/mod/dimensional-weather/version/1.1-1.20.1\",\"Apache-2.0 recorded in supplied assets\",\"minimum requirement documented; final intersection untested\",\"required_research\",\"Select the lowest exact common supported build\",\"Record artefact name and hash after acquisition.\"\n\"TC-004\",\"library\",\"iCommon API\",\"not pinned\",\"1.20.1 candidate\",\"Fabric\",\"Multiworld dependency\",\"https://github.com/IsaiahMC/multiworld\",\"LGPL-3.0 AND Unlicense recorded in supplied assets\",\"dependency existence recorded; exact release unresolved\",\"required_research\",\"Replace Multiworld or world method if dependency chain fails\",\"Do not assume a matching version.\"\n\"TC-005\",\"portal\",\"Immersive Portals\",\"5.2.0\",\"1.20.1\",\"Fabric\",\"See-through views, seamless crossing and exact destinations\",\"https://modrinth.com/mod/immersiveportals/version/5.2.0\",\"Apache-2.0\",\"documented individual support; combined stack untested\",\"first_portal_candidate\",\"Matched destination composite\",\"Asymmetric R4→R0/R0→R1 topology requires POC-005.\"\n\"TC-006\",\"worlds\",\"Multiworld\",\"1.12 beta\",\"1.20.1\",\"Fabric\",\"Separate overworld-like R0–R4 states\",\"https://modrinth.com/mod/multiworld/version/NfNQTHy9\",\"LGPL-3.0-or-later\",\"documented individual support; Immersive Portals interoperability untested\",\"first_world_candidate\",\"Separately sourced custom dimensions or shot-specific world copies\",\"Requires exact iCommon API resolution.\"\n\"TC-007\",\"weather\",\"Dimensional Weather\",\"1.1-1.20.1\",\"1.20.1\",\"Fabric or Quilt\",\"Keep R0 dry while R1 rains\",\"https://modrinth.com/mod/dimensional-weather/version/1.1-1.20.1\",\"MIT\",\"documented individual support; portal rendering untested\",\"first_weather_candidate\",\"Composite rainy destination plate\",\"Test alone before adding another weather-state mod.\"\n\"TC-008\",\"time_weather\",\"Dimension Level Data\",\"0.1.0-1.20.1\",\"1.20.1\",\"Fabric candidate\",\"Independent time and weather by dimension\",\"https://modrinth.com/mod/dimension-level-data/version/c2yUFutK\",\"not recorded from supplied evidence\",\"documented individual purpose; dependencies and coexistence untested\",\"conditional_alternative\",\"Fixed-time plates or post lighting\",\"Add only for a proven gap after TC-007.\"\n\"TC-009\",\"scripting\",\"Carpet\",\"1.4.112\",\"1.20 and 1.20.1\",\"Fabric\",\"Tick control and Scarpet sequencing\",\"https://modrinth.com/mod/carpet/version/1.4.112\",\"MIT\",\"documented individual support; production stack untested\",\"second_control_layer\",\"Vanilla datapack plus separate plates\",\"Do not add before minimum portal/world/weather proof.\"\n\"TC-010\",\"world_edit\",\"Axiom\",\"5.2.1\",\"1.20–1.20.1\",\"Fabric\",\"Build variants and manual region repair\",\"https://modrinth.com/mod/axiom/version/5.2.1\",\"not recorded from supplied evidence\",\"documented individual support; stack impact untested\",\"conditional_build_tool\",\"Structure templates and verified world copies\",\"Never use as the sole backup system.\"\n\"TC-011\",\"replay_camera\",\"Replay Mod\",\"exact 1.20.1 build not pinned\",\"1.20.1 candidate\",\"Fabric candidate\",\"Record performances and author later camera paths\",\"https://www.replaymod.com/\",\"not recorded from supplied evidence\",\"capability documented; exact-version intersection unverified\",\"camera_comparison_A\",\"Locked gameplay or separate camera tool\",\"Test portal visibility, worlds, entities and weather after baseline.\"\n\"TC-012\",\"camera_actor\",\"CinematicTools\",\"1.2.0+1.20.1\",\"1.20.1\",\"Fabric\",\"Authored cameras and possible actor presentation\",\"https://modrinth.com/mod/cinematictools/version/1.2.0%2B1.20.1\",\"not recorded from supplied evidence\",\"documented individual support; dependency chain unpinned\",\"camera_comparison_B\",\"Replay Mod or numerical spectator paths\",\"Compare separately rather than retaining both by default.\"\n\"TC-013\",\"library\",\"GeckoLib\",\"not pinned\",\"1.20.1 candidate\",\"Fabric\",\"CinematicTools dependency\",\"https://modrinth.com/mod/cinematictools/version/1.2.0%2B1.20.1\",\"not recorded\",\"dependency listed; exact release unresolved\",\"required_only_if_TC-012\",\"Reject TC-012 if chain introduces instability\",\"Resolve from exact release metadata.\"\n\"TC-014\",\"library\",\"CreativeCore\",\"not pinned\",\"1.20.1 candidate\",\"Fabric\",\"CinematicTools dependency\",\"https://modrinth.com/mod/cinematictools/version/1.2.0%2B1.20.1\",\"not recorded\",\"dependency listed; exact release unresolved\",\"required_only_if_TC-012\",\"Reject TC-012 if chain introduces instability\",\"Resolve from exact release metadata.\"\n\"TC-015\",\"performance\",\"Sodium\",\"not pinned\",\"1.20.1 candidate\",\"Fabric\",\"Optional frame-time improvement\",\"https://modrinth.com/mod/sodium\",\"not recorded from supplied evidence\",\"mentioned by portal release notes; exact intersection absent\",\"optional_test_last\",\"No-shader vanilla renderer\",\"Do not add before stable no-performance-mod capture.\"\n\"TC-016\",\"shader\",\"Iris\",\"not pinned\",\"1.20.1 candidate\",\"Fabric\",\"Optional shader path\",\"https://modrinth.com/mod/iris\",\"not recorded from supplied evidence\",\"mentioned by portal release notes; exact intersection absent\",\"could_cut\",\"Vanilla lighting and post grade\",\"First scope cut; no shader pack is selected.\"\n\"TC-017\",\"recording\",\"External or tool-integrated recorder\",\"not selected\",\"1.20.1 runtime\",\"not applicable\",\"Capture picture and guide audio\",\"official source not yet reviewed\",\"not recorded\",\"no exact tool, codec or performance evidence\",\"required_research\",\"Replay renderer or another officially sourced recorder\",\"Do not invent OBS version, codec success or recording performance.\"\n\"TC-018\",\"compositing\",\"Blender or conventional compositor\",\"not selected\",\"not applicable\",\"not applicable\",\"Camera match, portal card, depth masks and Scene 13 modules\",\"official source not yet reviewed\",\"not recorded\",\"workflow category only; no exact tool evidence\",\"conditional_fallback\",\"Locked 2D masks and matched dissolves\",\"Verify exact release, licence and plug-ins before use.\"\n\"TC-019\",\"game_alternative\",\"Minecraft Java Edition\",\"1.21.1\",\"1.21.1\",\"not selected\",\"Mandatory comparison baseline\",\"https://www.minecraft.net/\",\"Proprietary\",\"game target known; supporting intersection absent\",\"defer_pending_research\",\"Remain on 1.20.1\",\"No claim that 1.21.1 is incompatible.\"\n\"TC-020\",\"portal_alternative\",\"Immersive Portals for 1.21.1\",\"not established from supplied sources\",\"1.21.1\",\"Fabric candidate\",\"1.21.1 see-through portal comparison\",\"https://modrinth.com/project/zJpHMkdD\",\"not re-verified\",\"evidence gap\",\"research_before_migration\",\"TC-005 on 1.20.1 or composite\",\"Exact official release page required.\"\n\"TC-021\",\"world_alternative\",\"Multiple-world candidate for 1.21.1\",\"not established from supplied sources\",\"1.21.1\",\"Fabric candidate\",\"1.21.1 echo-world comparison\",\"https://modrinth.com/project/fgvoNDL1\",\"not re-verified\",\"evidence gap\",\"research_before_migration\",\"TC-006 on 1.20.1 or shot-specific copies\",\"Do not infer support from the general project page.\"\n\"TC-022\",\"weather_alternative\",\"Independent weather/time candidates for 1.21.1\",\"not established from supplied sources\",\"1.21.1\",\"Fabric candidate\",\"1.21.1 dry/rain comparison\",\"official exact release sources not supplied\",\"not re-verified\",\"evidence gap\",\"research_before_migration\",\"TC-007 or TC-008 on 1.20.1; composite weather\",\"Exact official releases and dependencies required.\"\n\"TC-023\",\"production_alternative\",\"Actor, camera, editor and replay intersection for 1.21.1\",\"not established from supplied sources\",\"1.21.1\",\"Fabric candidate\",\"Complete 1.21.1 production comparison\",\"official exact release sources not supplied\",\"not re-verified\",\"evidence gap\",\"research_before_migration\",\"1.20.1 candidates and controlled plates\",\"A 1.21.1 stack cannot be selected honestly from supplied evidence.\""},{"path":".studio/internal/production/scene-implementation-matrix.csv","content":"scene_id,script_requirement,preferred_method,minecraft_version,tool_or_mod,deterministic_control,camera_method,vfx_method,fallback,test_id,evidence_status,notes\n\"1\",\"R4 ridge return, smoke, purple cargo drop and MATCH PATH run without narration or portal audio\",\"Controlled R4 gameplay plate with separate smoke layer\",\"1.20.1 provisional\",\"Vanilla plus tpnm_take; compositor unselected\",\"Fixed night/weather, MP camera mark, hero path, tagged cargo marks and protected fire state\",\"Locked numerical MATCH PATH camera; raised 58-degree FOV\",\"Layer distant smoke and fire light only if live state is unstable\",\"Locked clean path plate plus isolated smoke/fire elements\",\"CONT-001; VFX-003\",\"planned_not_tested\",\"Capture with Scene 10 continuity where practical; no filename or take exists.\"\n\"2\",\"Lone R0 arrival, survival, wild-wolf intervention, taming, fishing, MOSS naming, routines and MATCH FRAME A\",\"Milestone world copies and short separately controlled action plates\",\"1.20.1 provisional\",\"Vanilla datapack first; Carpet/Scarpet conditional; Axiom conditional\",\"Separate wild, tamed-unnamed and named states; fixed skeleton marks; controlled fishing insert; exact MF-A marks\",\"Locked MATCH PATH arrival, short montage tracks and locked 52-degree MATCH FRAME A\",\"Only concealed joins and graphic inserts; no generated imagery\",\"Separate threat, intervention, taming and naming plates joined causally\",\"MEC-001; MEC-002; MEC-003; CONT-001; GFX-001\",\"planned_not_tested\",\"Collar and name cannot appear early; preserve one future narration recording for Scenes 2 and 13.\"\n\"3\",\"Ordinary descent, granite seam, iron-caused turn, crying-frame reveal, rainy parallax and continuous crossing with Moss\",\"Live Immersive Portals view if minimum proof passes\",\"1.20.1 provisional\",\"Immersive Portals 5.2.0; world/weather candidates conditional\",\"Fixed seam/iron structures, player and Moss threshold marks, controlled chunks and weather\",\"Descending follow, slow reveal, four-block lateral track and threshold follow\",\"Destination plate, tracked frame mask, tear particles and audio transition if live path fails\",\"Matched R0/R1 plates with threshold occlusion or controlled cut for Moss\",\"POC-002; POC-003; POC-004; MEC-003\",\"documented_individual_support_only; integrated_not_tested\",\"Portal sound starts only after visible reveal.\"\n\"4\",\"R1 rainy arrival, absent surface home, dry-looking return view and one cobblestone marker\",\"Separate R1 master-derived state with fixed rain\",\"1.20.1 provisional\",\"Immersive Portals 5.2.0; Multiworld 1.12; Dimensional Weather 1.1 candidates\",\"Fixed rain/time, R1 geometry, player/Moss arrival marks and one-block marker structure\",\"Matched seam arrival, environmental surface track and locked foot insert\",\"Composite rain/light/audio if portal weather does not render\",\"R1 destination plate with matched source frame and hidden crossing cut\",\"POC-003; POC-004; CONT-002\",\"planned_not_tested\",\"The surface difference must be physical, not grade-only.\"\n\"5\",\"R2 first missing marker, deliberate L marker, R3 second absence and ECHOES conclusion\",\"Master-derived R2/R3 states with structure-controlled marker variants\",\"1.20.1 provisional\",\"Vanilla tpnm_take; Axiom only for building\",\"Bare-foot, one-block and L-plus-torch structures; fixed journal/block-count inserts\",\"Exact locked frame-foot camera repeated in R1, R2 and R3; short surface geography shot\",\"Ash particles may be a separate restrained layer\",\"Use locked clean plates and editorial cuts rather than live consecutive crossings\",\"CONT-002; GFX-001; POC-005\",\"planned_not_tested\",\"Hold each absence long enough to register; same coordinates are crew evidence only.\"\n\"6\",\"Archive habits, paired journals, seven Atlas instructions, failing mouth, gravel blockage and forced crossing\",\"Compact R3 set plus separately controlled insert and portal-failure plates\",\"1.20.1 provisional\",\"Vanilla tpnm_take; Immersive Portals candidate; graphics/compositor unselected\",\"Page-order cue, fixed desk props, gravel structures, shrinking-mouth timing and Moss exit mark\",\"Slow archive survey, 35–40-degree locked inserts and wide threshold exit\",\"Contracting destination mask, sound-layer dropout and controlled gravel state\",\"Static graphic pages and matched portal composite with concealed crossing\",\"GFX-001; VFX-001; POC-003\",\"planned_not_tested\",\"Use only Script-approved Atlas wording; no cosmology additions.\"\n\"7\",\"R4 dry arrival, projected-block fade, ordinary-fire failure, surface marker and first roof\",\"Fresh R4 milestone with staged incomplete-mouth structure\",\"1.20.1 provisional\",\"Vanilla tpnm_take; Immersive Portals candidate\",\"Fixed dry morning, complete-to-incomplete frame structures, failed-fire cue, marker and shelter module\",\"Matched arrival then static collapse and restrained rise to surface\",\"Fade projected upper blocks and destination image softly\",\"Cut from complete arrival plate to inert-frame plate; no live collapse required\",\"POC-003; VFX-001; ACT-001\",\"planned_not_tested\",\"The collapse is quiet and non-explosive.\"\n\"8\",\"Passage of time, shared routines, hearth, rug growth, conventional portal trips and slow material preparation\",\"Repeated locked compositions across protected R4 milestones\",\"1.20.1 provisional\",\"Vanilla tpnm_take; Axiom conditional; conventional portal vanilla\",\"Build-state structures, Moss marks, sit/follow/feed cues, rug state IDs and fixed seasonal light plates\",\"Locked exterior, domestic wide, short bridge follows and ledger inserts\",\"Weather and time transitions through cuts; no ominous fire emphasis\",\"Reduce montage angles while preserving every causal domestic beat\",\"MEC-003; MEC-004; CONT-004\",\"planned_not_tested\",\"Final rug square creates the proposed fire origin but remains affectionate in presentation.\"\n\"9\",\"Final ledger entries, routine feed/sit/bark, conventional departure and first rug flame\",\"Controlled Moss routine plus separate room/fire-origin plate\",\"1.20.1 provisional\",\"Vanilla tpnm_take; audio recorder unselected\",\"Exact Moss/rug marks, feed cue, two sit gestures, isolated bark sync and fixed ignition mark\",\"Static ledger insert, measured two-shot and locked room wide\",\"Composite or progressive first-flame state if spread timing varies\",\"Join a clean Moss hold to a separate ignition plate after portal audio fades\",\"AUD-001; MEC-003; MEC-004\",\"planned_not_tested\",\"Scene 12 must reuse this exact future bark performance; none exists yet.\"\n\"10\",\"Resume MATCH PATH, water and steam, blocked doorway, wall breach, empty room, burn fan, search and Atlas choice\",\"Protected burning and burned R4 copies with separate hazard plates\",\"1.20.1 provisional\",\"Vanilla tpnm_take; Axiom conditional; compositor unselected\",\"Exact path continuation, water cue, falling-timber state, removable wall, search marks and forbidden-item cleanup\",\"Locked MATCH PATH, static doorway, slow burned-room settle and route montage\",\"Controlled steam/smoke/fire layers and progressive burn states\",\"Art-directed burned state retaining tested origin and fan; separate search plates\",\"CONT-001; MEC-004; VFX-003; EDIT-002\",\"planned_not_tested\",\"No body, collar drop, death message or locating bark.\"\n\"11\",\"Granite-seam return, sub-second creeper route plant, frame completion, charged anchor, topology insert and reachable baffle\",\"Sacrificial final-chamber copy with state-based construction\",\"1.20.1 provisional\",\"Vanilla tpnm_take; Carpet/Scarpet conditional; graphics tool unselected\",\"Connected ledge/landing marks, tagged creeper hold, frame-state structures, anchor appearance, baffle/reach marks and journal storage\",\"Brief first-person descent, locked labour fragments, insert and measured baffle lateral\",\"No echo activation; optional darkness mask only\",\"Separate creeper-glimpse plate and construction plates\",\"MEC-005; MEC-006; CONT-003; GFX-001\",\"planned_not_tested\",\"The protagonist equips flint and steel but does not ignite.\"\n\"12\",\"Remembered bark, choice, falling creeper, close hiss, fatal blast, black interval, aftermath, anchor flash and delayed portal activation\",\"Separate controlled performance, fall, hiss, blast, aftermath and VFX plates\",\"1.20.1 provisional\",\"Vanilla tpnm_take; Carpet/Scarpet conditional; compositor unselected\",\"Exact bark asset reuse, action tick cues, tagged creeper route, sacrificial blast copy, protagonist-free aftermath and approved item marks\",\"Locked medium before death; literal black frame; locked external aftermath\",\"Explosion/smoke, violet flash, particles and resolving R0 view built as ordered layers\",\"Sound-led fatal cut plus art-directed aftermath; no continuous simulation required\",\"MEC-005; MEC-006; VFX-002; AUD-001\",\"planned_not_tested\",\"Creeper-triggered echo activation is invented canon. No narration after death.\"\n\"13\",\"Audience-only approach, R0 crossing, stylised vertical ascent, exact MATCH FRAME A repeat and waiting R0 mouth\",\"Matched portal plates and modular vertical transition\",\"1.20.1 provisional\",\"Immersive Portals candidate; Blender/compositor unselected; tpnm_take\",\"Protected R0 established-pair state, exact MF-A camera/lighting/equipment/Moss marks and one narration master\",\"External frame approach, seam crossing, vertical modular move and locked MF-A\",\"Portal card, stone/soil layer dissolves and final R1 rain view\",\"Shorter environmental dissolves using the Scene 2 source image where editorially feasible\",\"CONT-001; EDIT-001; AUD-001; POC-003\",\"planned_not_tested\",\"Must not imply survival, consciousness or a surface hum.\""},{"path":".studio/internal/production/test-matrix.csv","content":"test_id,capability,scene_ids,stack,procedure,pass_criteria,failure_evidence,fallback,status,notes\n\"VER-120\",\"Resolve exact 1.20.1 loader and dependency chain\",\"3-13\",\"Minecraft 1.20.1; Fabric; proposed candidates\",\"Review official exact release metadata for Java, Fabric Loader, Fabric API, iCommon API, GeckoLib and CreativeCore; record versions, URLs, licences and dependency constraints before acquisition\",\"One non-contradictory exact candidate chain is documented without inferred compatibility\",\"Missing release, conflicting requirement or unresolved licence recorded in source ledger\",\"Remove optional components or replace the component with the unresolved chain\",\"not_run\",\"No artefact or hash exists yet.\"\n\"VER-121\",\"Establish an exact 1.21.1 comparison stack\",\"3-13\",\"Minecraft 1.21.1; official project release pages\",\"Research exact releases for portal, worlds, weather/time, Carpet, editor, replay/camera and dependencies; compare publication dates, licences and requirements\",\"At least one exact candidate per critical category with a coherent paper dependency chain\",\"No exact release, incompatible published requirements or absent primary source\",\"Retain provisional 1.20.1 baseline\",\"not_run\",\"Do not claim that 1.21.1 lacks support merely because evidence is absent.\"\n\"POC-001\",\"Clean profile launch and reload\",\"3-13\",\"Minecraft 1.20.1; pinned Java; Fabric Loader/API; Immersive Portals only\",\"Launch isolated profile, create test world and portal, save, exit, reload and repeat; retain latest log and exact artefact hashes\",\"Two launches and reloads complete with portal present and no blocker-level errors\",\"Crash report, latest log, mod list and exact reproduction steps\",\"Replace only the failing component or use composite portal route\",\"not_run\",\"Minimum stack precedes all other mods.\"\n\"POC-002\",\"Separate same-base echo geography\",\"3-7,13\",\"POC-001 plus Multiworld 1.12 and pinned iCommon API\",\"Create R0 and R1 from one seed/configuration or copied master; record world IDs and compare seam, cave, surface column and coordinates before and after reload\",\"Both states remain independently editable and hero geography aligns for intended shots\",\"World IDs, coordinate screenshots, mismatch measurements and reload log\",\"Use controlled region copies or matched hero-location shells\",\"not_run\",\"Multiworld/portal destination interoperability is included only after basic world proof.\"\n\"POC-003\",\"Portal view, parallax and player crossing\",\"3,4,6,7,13\",\"POC-002 plus Immersive Portals 5.2.0\",\"Record static view, four-block lateral move and threshold crossing in both directions; inspect clipping, parallax, load discontinuity and reload\",\"Destination perspective responds correctly, source foreground occludes correctly and player crossing is editorially usable twice after reload\",\"Video, transform data, logs and frame-by-frame defect notes\",\"Matched destination plate, tracked mask and concealed cut\",\"not_run\",\"Do not include wolf until player test passes.\"\n\"POC-004\",\"Independent dry R0 and rainy R1 weather/time\",\"3,4\",\"POC-003 plus Dimensional Weather 1.1 or Dimension Level Data tested separately\",\"Fix time; set R0 clear and R1 rain; view R1 from R0, cross, reload and repeat without shaders\",\"Rain, destination light, waterfall and state persist while R0 remains dry; audio can be isolated\",\"Source/destination stills, weather commands, logs and mismatch notes\",\"Composite rainy R1 plate and rebuild audio in post\",\"not_run\",\"One weather method at a time.\"\n\"POC-005\",\"Asymmetric R4→R0 view with R0→R1 entry\",\"3,4,12,13\",\"Validated portal/world baseline\",\"Create minimal R0, R1 and R4 portals; record every face and entry direction before and after reload\",\"R4 shows and enters R0 as required while the scripted R0 entry continues to R1, or a documented shot-specific configuration reproduces both states\",\"Destination table, recordings, commands and unwanted return-mouth evidence\",\"Shot-specific portal states or composited views\",\"not_run\",\"Simultaneous live topology is preferred but not mandatory if editorial continuity remains exact.\"\n\"ACT-001\",\"Datapack setup-arm-action-reset-cleanup lifecycle\",\"2,7-12\",\"Vanilla functions, tags, markers, scoreboards and structures\",\"Run one non-destructive take twice, reload, then run again; inspect rules, marks, actors and cleanup selectors\",\"Each cycle returns to the same armed state; no untagged or persistent entity changes; rules restore on cleanup\",\"Before/after data, logs and list of leaked entities or state drift\",\"Add Carpet/Scarpet for the isolated timing gap or use world-state copies\",\"not_run\",\"Custom mod is not an initial fallback.\"\n\"CAM-001\",\"Camera and replay compatibility\",\"1-13\",\"Validated minimum stack; Replay Mod and CinematicTools in separate copied profiles\",\"Record one locked shot, one lateral portal path, one actor take and one cross-world event with each candidate; save/reload and render or capture\",\"Numerical repeatability, correct portal/interior/entities/weather and playable output without blocker defects\",\"Logs, replay defects, missing entity list and frame-time comparison\",\"Vanilla locked camera, spectator path or matched plates\",\"not_run\",\"Retain the simpler passing camera route.\"\n\"PERF-001\",\"Stable no-shader capture baseline and optional rendering additions\",\"3,4,12,13\",\"Validated portal/camera stack; recording tool unselected\",\"Measure static, lateral and crossing shots without shaders; then add Sodium and Iris individually only from exact pins\",\"Playable capture at the selected resolution/frame rate with no visible portal corruption and acceptable recorded frame pacing\",\"Frame-time trace, capture inspection, crash/log evidence and exact settings\",\"Reduce portal recursion/render distance; remove shaders; composite destination\",\"not_run\",\"No target is claimed until hardware and recorder are selected.\"\n\"MEC-001\",\"Skeleton threat, wild-wolf intervention and taming transition\",\"2\",\"tpnm_take; vanilla mobs; Carpet conditional\",\"Arm skeleton, wild wolf and protagonist on fixed marks; release scheduled plates; perform visible bones offer and inspect state before/after taming\",\"Threat, intervention and cause-to-taming read clearly; no collar/name appears early; reset repeats\",\"Path deviations, targeting evidence, state screenshots and reset defects\",\"Separate skeleton, wolf response and taming plates\",\"not_run\",\"Do not rely on natural targeting RNG.\"\n\"MEC-002\",\"Fishing-to-name-tag and anvil MOSS chain\",\"2\",\"tpnm_take; vanilla fishing/anvil; controlled inventory insert\",\"Stage a fishing action and readable acquisition/pick-up insert; show anvil label `MOSS`; apply to correct tamed unnamed wolf\",\"Edit preserves fishing as cause and the name appears only after application\",\"Unreadable catch, early name, wrong wolf state or inventory mismatch\",\"Controlled catch/pick-up insert joined to genuine fishing action\",\"not_run\",\"This is a scheduling control, not a claim about catch probability.\"\n\"MEC-003\",\"Moss states, routines and portal crossing\",\"2-4,6-9,13\",\"Validated portal baseline; tpnm_take\",\"Test wild, tamed-unnamed and named states; follow, wait, sit, second sit gesture, feed and crossing; reload and inspect owner/name/collar/health/pose\",\"Every required state and short action is repeatable; named Moss crosses and retains data after reload\",\"Entity data, screenshots, path logs and duplication/loss evidence\",\"Destination-side Moss plate with concealed handoff; shorter controlled actions\",\"not_run\",\"Persistent Moss cannot be silently replaced.\"\n\"MEC-004\",\"Rug-origin fire path and progressive reset\",\"8-10\",\"Exact backed-up shared-room geometry; tpnm_take\",\"Run repeated fire mechanics tests from the defined final green square with timing recorded; restore from pre-fire state after each run\",\"Origin and route are legible and at least one method produces a controllable rug-to-timber fan without contaminating the master\",\"Before/after states, tick timings, spread variance and restore verification\",\"Progressive art-directed states retaining tested origin and burn fan\",\"not_run\",\"Natural RNG is not a production dependency.\"\n\"MEC-005\",\"Connected creeper ledge, peripheral plant, fall and hiss timing\",\"11,12\",\"Sacrificial final chamber; tpnm_take; Carpet conditional\",\"Verify physical ledge-to-landing route; capture sub-second edge at delivery size; repeat fall/landing/hiss with exact marks\",\"Route is discoverable on rewatch, unobtrusive first time and lands behind the protagonist at the required cue\",\"Route diagram, failed paths, timing and review notes\",\"Separate glimpse, fall, landing, hiss and reaction plates\",\"not_run\",\"No sting or protagonist reaction in Scene 11.\"\n\"MEC-006\",\"Fatal blast and readable aftermath geometry\",\"12\",\"Sacrificial final chamber; controlled creeper\",\"Test difficulty, equipment, distance, frame/baffle damage and item scatter; never use the only set state\",\"Blast can motivate death and an aftermath plate can retain recognisable frame/baffle geography without forbidden items\",\"Damage values, geometry comparisons, item list and restore proof\",\"Black-frame fatal cut and art-directed protagonist-free aftermath\",\"not_run\",\"No claim that the frame naturally survives as scripted.\"\n\"VFX-001\",\"Portal failure and quiet R4 collapse\",\"6,7\",\"Live portal candidate or compositor\",\"Create stable, contracting and inert states; review the R3 forced exit and R4 soft fade with sound layers\",\"State change is readable, non-explosive and does not resemble ordinary Nether behaviour\",\"Review export and notes on clipping, timing or confusion\",\"Matched plates with animated mask and projected-block fade\",\"not_run\",\"Portal exposition stays within Script labels.\"\n\"VFX-002\",\"Delayed anchor flash, particles and R0 view\",\"12\",\"Locked aftermath plate; compositor unselected\",\"Assemble black interval, smoke, one violet flash, first particle, second particle and gradual destination view in Script order\",\"Viewers read delayed activation after death and do not infer a vanilla mechanic or survival\",\"Timing export, comprehension notes and continuity defects\",\"Simpler locked dissolve into the active frame\",\"not_run\",\"No narration follows death.\"\n\"VFX-003\",\"Smoke, fire, water and steam continuity\",\"1,10\",\"Protected R4 states; controlled plates\",\"Compare distant smoke, path fire light, doorway water, steam, falling timber and breached-room plate across locked cameras\",\"Effects preserve geography and do not obscure the empty-place/burn-fan evidence\",\"Layer breakdown and continuity overlay\",\"Reduce live effects and use isolated layers\",\"not_run\",\"Avoid resolving Moss through background debris or sound.\"\n\"CONT-001\",\"MATCH PATH and MATCH FRAME A repeatability\",\"1,2,10,13\",\"Protected R0/R4 states; chosen camera tool\",\"Record numerical transforms, FOV, lighting, marks and reference overlays; repeat each after reload\",\"Path frames align within the approved overlay tolerance and MF-A uses identical picture design and one narration asset\",\"Overlay difference images, transform records and state mismatch list\",\"Reuse source plate or rebuild dressing around one locked camera\",\"not_run\",\"Tolerance must be set by human review after greyboxing.\"\n\"CONT-002\",\"Frame-foot and granite-seam continuity\",\"3-6\",\"R0-R3 master-derived states\",\"Capture seam and left-foot reference from every echo; overlay silhouette and marker positions\",\"Natural seam remains recognisable and marker presence/absence is unambiguous\",\"Overlay and mismatch notes\",\"Matched hero shell or corrective rebuild\",\"not_run\",\"Do not repair with colour grading alone.\"\n\"CONT-003\",\"Final-frame asymmetry and creeper route geography\",\"3,11,12\",\"R0 receiving mouth; R4 source chamber\",\"Compare frame dimensions/asymmetries and trace ledge to landing in plan/elevation\",\"R4 source visually matches R0 mouth and ledge connection is physically readable\",\"Measurements, overlays and route recording\",\"Shot-specific matched shell and separate fall plate\",\"not_run\",\"Story topology is fictional; physical visual match is required.\"\n\"CONT-004\",\"Homestead milestone continuity\",\"7-10\",\"Protected R4 world copies\",\"Review shelter, home, rug stages, pre-fire, burning and burned states against a prop/state checklist\",\"Each later state follows visibly from the previous one and destructive states restore from verified sources\",\"State checklist, restore hashes or copy identifiers and discrepancies\",\"Rebuild only the affected module from the protected milestone\",\"not_run\",\"No completed world state exists.\"\n\"AUD-001\",\"Narration/bark reuse and portal-audio boundaries\",\"2,3,9,12,13\",\"Isolated audio stems; recorder/edit system unselected\",\"Place one mining-departure recording in Scenes 2 and 13; reuse one Scene 9 bark in Scene 12; review Scenes 2–3 and 13 for surface portal sound\",\"Audio assets are byte-identical where required; no surface hum; remembered bark reads as subjective\",\"Waveform/file comparison and full-sequence mix notes\",\"Replace both placements from one approved master and rebuild stems\",\"not_run\",\"No audio recording exists.\"\n\"GFX-001\",\"Journal, Atlas, ledger, title and name readability\",\"2,5,6,9-11\",\"Original graphics; delivery-size review\",\"Create only Script-approved pages, hold at planned FOV/duration and review at delivery size without narration\",\"Required symbols, markers and seven Atlas instructions are legible in order with no superseded wording\",\"Still/motion review and list of misread labels\",\"Larger, fewer or longer locked inserts\",\"not_run\",\"No graphic asset exists.\"\n\"EDIT-001\",\"Scene 13 omniscient reading and loop clarity\",\"13\",\"Text board then greybox animatic\",\"Show protagonist-free aftermath, external frame approach, environmental ascent and MF-A repeat to reviewers without explanatory additions\",\"Reviewers understand the protagonist died, camera is audience access and R0 entry will continue to R1\",\"Anonymous comprehension responses and confusion notes\",\"Shorten to explicit environmental dissolves and an external establishing plate\",\"not_run\",\"Do not add narration after death.\"\n\"EDIT-002\",\"Moss fate remains unresolved\",\"9,10,12,13\",\"Storyboard, edit and sound review\",\"Inspect every picture and sound for body, collar drop, death text, locating bark, implication of escape or final-R0 survival proof\",\"Review confirms only absence in R4 and earlier Moss in R0\",\"Timestamped list of offending evidence\",\"Remove or replace affected plate, item or sound\",\"not_run\",\"This is a canon gate.\"\n\"STB-001\",\"Five-panel storyboard model consistency\",\"2,3,10,13\",\"Real Minecraft/Blender greyboxes; ChatGPT Images 2.0 and FLUX.2 Pro comparison\",\"Transform the five approved reference cases into one graphite-and-ink style; overlay outputs and score identity, geometry, props, ratio and continuity\",\"All five preserve essential composition and canon without invented evidence; human approves one model\",\"Prompts, source frames, overlays and failure notes\",\"Retain text/greybox boards or test alternative model\",\"not_run\",\"No image may be generated until the human triggers the later test.\""},{"path":".studio/internal/production/storyboard-panels.csv","content":"panel_id,scene_id,shot_id,order,frame_description,composition,camera,subject_blocking,environment,lighting,movement,transition,audio,continuity,generation_reference,status\n\"P01-01\",\"1\",\"S01-001\",\"1\",\"Exact moment: the protagonist reaches the R4 ridge crest and first sees smoke; capture purpose is to reveal danger before the house and make the purple cargo visible.\",\"TL dark sky; TM smoke plume; TR ridge silhouette; ML empty slope; MM protagonist and cargo; MR distant fire glow; BL path stones; BM crest grass; BR descent path\",\"MP local camera at (-4,2.6,-8), height 2.6 blocks, 62-degree FOV, facing (0,1,10)\",\"Hero at (0,0,0), faces +Z towards house, eyeline to smoke at (0,8,18); cargo in both hands; no Moss\",\"Foreground ridge grass and path; midground hero; background smoke and partly hidden homestead\",\"Moon/key from upper camera-left; orange fire bounce from background-right\",\"Hero moves from lower-middle towards centre, then stops; smoke rises vertically and drifts right\",\"Hard cut in action coverage to P01-02\",\"Wind, hurried steps, distant fire; no narration, music or portal sound\",\"R4 night kit, crying obsidian and glowstone present; house not fully revealed\",\"Later input must be an actual R4 greybox; transform only; no image exists\",\"planned_no_image\"\n\"P01-02\",\"1\",\"S01-002\",\"2\",\"Exact moment: cargo hits the path and the protagonist runs towards the burning homestead from MATCH PATH; purpose is the Scene 1-to-2 motion match.\",\"TL night sky; TM smoke; TR tree edge; ML empty ridge; MM hero running away; MR distant house glow; BL cargo; BM path line; BR grass\",\"MP-C at (0,2.2,-10), height 2.2, 58-degree FOV, level, facing +Z; camera static\",\"Hero starts (0,0,-2), faces +Z and runs to (0,0,8); eyeline house at Z+18; cargo fixed at (-1,0,-1)\",\"Foreground cargo/path; midground running hero; background developed homestead and smoke\",\"Fire backlight from upper centre-right; weak moon from left\",\"Hero arrow away from camera towards upper-middle; no camera move\",\"Jump cut on matched leg position to P02-01\",\"Footsteps, wind and fire only\",\"MATCH PATH numerical transform, path centreline and direction; preserve for Scenes 2 and 10\",\"Later input: locked R4 plate and R0 counterpart; capture purpose match cut; no image exists\",\"planned_no_image\"\n\"P02-01\",\"2\",\"S02-001\",\"1\",\"Exact moment: morning replaces night and the lone protagonist walks into the untouched clearing on the same path; purpose is title and chronology misdirection.\",\"TL pale sky; TM morning light; TR birches; ML untouched grass; MM lone hero; MR ravine-side trees; BL empty path; BM path line; BR flowers\",\"MP-C at (0,2.2,-10), height 2.2, 58-degree FOV, level, facing +Z; identical to P01-02\",\"Hero at the matched leg pose near (0,0,-2), faces +Z, eyeline to clearing; simple kit; no wolf and no structures\",\"Foreground empty path; midground lone hero; background fresh clearing and birches\",\"Sun from upper camera-left at planned R0 morning angle\",\"Hero continues away from camera at walking pace along +Z\",\"Jump cut from P01-02; title appears over uncluttered upper-left\",\"Morning wind, leaves and footsteps; no portal sound\",\"MATCH PATH exact camera/path; R0 fresh state; protagonist arrives alone\",\"Later input: actual locked R0 greybox paired with P01-02; no image exists\",\"planned_no_image\"\n\"P02-02\",\"2\",\"S02-002\",\"2\",\"Exact moment: the protagonist sits at the overlook after lowering his pack; purpose is to show a voluntary choice to stay.\",\"TL birch canopy; TM bright sky; TR distant ridge; ML water; MM seated hero and pack; MR grass clearing; BL near grass; BM ravine lip; BR path continuing away\",\"CL-C at (-6,2.8,-8), height 2.8, 64-degree FOV, facing overlook O=(0,1,0)\",\"Hero at O=(0,0,0), seated facing +Z/right towards water; eyeline to sunlit water at (4,-4,12); pack at (-1,0,0)\",\"Foreground grass/ravine lip; midground hero and clearing; background water, birches and possible onward path\",\"Morning sun from upper-left across water towards lower-right\",\"Hero lowers vertically, then remains still; leaves move rightward\",\"Dissolve or cut into early-game montage\",\"Narration about being able to keep walking; wind and leaves\",\"Fresh R0; stitched journal remains mostly blank; no wolf\",\"Later input: actual overlook greybox; capture purpose establish chosen home; no image exists\",\"planned_no_image\"\n\"P02-03\",\"2\",\"S02-003\",\"3\",\"Exact moment: a wild wolf attacks the skeleton threatening the unarmoured protagonist; purpose is the causal rescue before taming.\",\"TL birch leaves; TM skeleton bow; TR tree trunks; ML hero recoiling; MM skeleton; MR wild wolf entering; BL dropped arrow; BM grass; BR crop edge\",\"S2-A at (-7,1.7,-5), height 1.7, 66-degree FOV, facing (0,1,0)\",\"Hero at (-2,0,0) faces skeleton at (0,0,1), eyeline chest-high; skeleton faces hero; wild wolf at (3,0,1) faces left towards skeleton; wolf has no collar/name\",\"Foreground grass/arrow; midground three actors; background birches and shelter edge\",\"Night torch/key from camera-left; moon rim from upper-right\",\"Skeleton draws towards left; wolf arrow right-to-left; hero shifts back towards lower-left\",\"Sharp montage cut from earlier survival work; cut on wolf impact to aftermath\",\"Skeleton rattle, bow tension, wolf growl; narration about arrows and intervention\",\"Wild wolf state only; no hearts, collar or name\",\"Five-panel model test action case; use actual three-actor greybox; no image exists\",\"planned_no_image\"\n\"P02-04\",\"2\",\"S02-004\",\"4\",\"Exact moment: after the skeleton is gone, the protagonist offers recovered bones and hearts rise; purpose is to connect aid, bones and taming.\",\"TL birch leaves; TM hearts; TR shelter edge; ML hero crouched; MM bones between; MR wolf; BL tool lowered; BM grass; BR arrow remains\",\"S2-T at (-4,1.4,-4), height 1.4, 52-degree FOV, facing midpoint (0,1,0)\",\"Hero at (-1.5,0,0) faces right, hand extended; wolf at (1.5,0,0) faces left and looks at bones; collar appears only after heart cue\",\"Foreground lowered tool and grass; midground hero/bones/wolf; background birches and shelter\",\"Soft dawn or torch fill from camera-left; no dramatic rim\",\"Hero hand moves right; wolf steps left; hearts move upward\",\"Cut from intervention aftermath; later dissolve into routines\",\"Quiet paws, bone use and taming cue\",\"Transition from wild to tamed unnamed; no `Moss` label\",\"Later input: actual taming-state greybox; capture purpose causal relationship; no image exists\",\"planned_no_image\"\n\"P02-05\",\"2\",\"S02-004\",\"5\",\"Exact moment: the protagonist applies the anvil-labelled MOSS name tag to the tamed unnamed wolf; purpose is the final identity-state transition.\",\"TL shelter wall; TM anvil top; TR journal shelf; ML protagonist arm; MM MOSS tag; MR wolf head; BL fishing rod; BM anvil base; BR green bank glimpse\",\"S2-N at (-3,1.5,-3), height 1.5, 42-degree FOV, facing anvil/wolf midpoint\",\"Hero at (-1,0,0) faces right; tamed unnamed wolf at (1,0,0) faces left and looks to hand; `Moss` name appears only after application\",\"Foreground fishing rod/anvil; midground hand, tag and wolf; background shelter and green bank\",\"Daylight from upper-right window; small warm fill from left\",\"Hand arrow right towards wolf; name rises above wolf after contact\",\"Match-on-action from anvil insert; cut to established routines\",\"Anvil sound, name-tag use and family narration\",\"Fishing cause already shown; collar present; name begins here\",\"Five-panel relationship/prop test; source must be actual greybox; no image exists\",\"planned_no_image\"\n\"P02-06\",\"2\",\"S02-005\",\"6\",\"Exact moment: at MATCH FRAME A the packed protagonist tightens the strap and named Moss arrives beside him; purpose is the exact Scene 13 repeat.\",\"TL morning sky; TM birch canopy; TR ridge; ML ravine opening; MM hero tightening pack; MR named Moss; BL path down; BM grass mark; BR water glint\",\"MF-A camera at (-5,2.2,-7), height 2.2, 52-degree FOV, facing (0,1,2)\",\"Hero at (0,0,0) faces three-quarter right towards descent, eyeline to first ledge; Moss at (2,0,0.5) faces same direction and looks down; name visible only if delivery framing permits\",\"Foreground ravine lip/path; midground pair; background birches, water and morning sky\",\"Sun from upper-left; identical direction required in Scene 13\",\"Hero hand tightens down; Moss trots left-to-right into mark; both then move down and away\",\"Cut into Scene 3 descent; exact visual later repeated in P13-04\",\"One reusable narration take: Below the hill was only another day's work. They went together.\",\"MATCH FRAME A camera, FOV, light, kit, journal, Moss mark and action\",\"Five-panel exact-match case paired with P13-04; no image exists\",\"planned_no_image\"\n\"P03-01\",\"3\",\"S03-001\",\"1\",\"Exact moment: the descent reaches the forked granite seam and exposed iron continues around the next turn; purpose is to establish geography and cause discovery.\",\"TL cave roof; TM water stream; TR placed blocks; ML seam upper fork; MM hero journalling; MR iron vein leading right; BL Moss waiting; BM ledge; BR dark turn\",\"PC-D at (-6,2.4,-10), height 2.4, 62-degree FOV, facing seam centre (0,2,0)\",\"Hero at (0,0,0) faces wall then turns right along iron; Moss at (-2,0,-1) waits facing hero; eyeline follows iron towards +X/+Z turn\",\"Foreground ledge and Moss; midground hero/seam/iron; background dark turn\",\"Torch key from lower camera-left; cool water light from upper-centre\",\"Water falls down; hero movement turns centre-to-right; later Moss follows\",\"Cut from MF-A descent; cut on hero rounding turn\",\"Mining, water and paws; no portal audio\",\"Forked seam introduced as ordinary marker; iron is causal route\",\"Later input: actual master-ravine greybox; no image exists\",\"planned_no_image\"\n\"P03-02\",\"3\",\"S03-002\",\"2\",\"Exact moment: the complete crying frame first enters view beyond the iron turn; purpose is the impossible-object reveal.\",\"TL dark roof; TM crying particles; TR dry stone; ML iron edge; MM frame opening; MR rainy destination; BL hero shoulder; BM cave floor; BR Moss edge\",\"PC-R at (-5,1.8,-7), height 1.8, 58-degree FOV, facing frame centre (0,2,0)\",\"Hero at (-2,0,-4) faces +Z to frame; Moss behind at (-3,0,-5); both eyelines centre; no reflected hero in portal\",\"Foreground iron corner/hero shoulder; midground crying frame; background rainy R1 cave visible through centre\",\"Warm torch from camera-left on source; cool rainy destination light from frame\",\"Camera reveals right around corner; particles move through frame towards far face\",\"Corner reveal from P03-01; hold before narration\",\"Mining sound drops; low echo texture starts only after frame is visible\",\"Frame dimensions/asymmetry reference; source remains dry\",\"Later input: actual portal greybox or composite design; no image exists\",\"planned_no_image\"\n\"P03-03\",\"3\",\"S03-003\",\"3\",\"Exact moment: the camera tracks laterally and destination geometry shifts with parallax; purpose is the central live-portal proof.\",\"TL source ceiling; TM frame top; TR destination rain; ML source wall; MM transparent opening; MR destination seam/water