\",\"Publication-rights review not recorded\",\"Wild; tamed unnamed; named\",\"Scenes 2–13\",\"planned\",\"Track owner, collar, name, health, sit/follow and position.\"\n\"CHAR-003\",\"Skeleton action profile\",\"in_game_character\",\"Minecraft entity under SW-001\",\"Publication-rights review not recorded\",\"1.20.1 candidate\",\"Scene 2 threat and bones cause\",\"planned\",\"Controlled plates; natural targeting not required.\"\n\"CHAR-004\",\"Creeper continuity profile\",\"in_game_character\",\"Minecraft entity under SW-001\",\"Publication-rights review not recorded\",\"1.20.1 candidate\",\"Scene 11 route and Scene 12 interruption\",\"planned\",\"Route, damage and aftermath untested.\"\n\"PROP-001\",\"Clean survey journal pages\",\"original_graphic\",\"Luan planned\",\"Authorship record pending creation\",\"Not created\",\"Symbols, coordinates, markers and ECHOES\",\"not_created\",\"Stitched corner, ravine symbol and arrow-shaped seven.\"\n\"PROP-002\",\"Weeping Atlas pages\",\"original_graphic\",\"Luan planned\",\"Authorship record pending creation\",\"Not created\",\"Seven Script-approved inserts\",\"not_created\",\"No superseded direct-discharge wording.\"\n\"PROP-003\",\"Material ledger\",\"original_graphic\",\"Luan planned\",\"Authorship record pending creation\",\"Not created\",\"Scenes 8–10 supply continuity\",\"not_created\",\"Counts and two final entries must be readable.\"\n\"PROP-004\",\"MOSS name-tag chain\",\"in_game_prop_set\",\"Minecraft plus planned capture\",\"Publication-rights review not recorded\",\"1.20.1 candidate\",\"Fishing, anvil and naming cause\",\"planned\",\"No recorded catch or probability result.\"\n\"SET-001\",\"Moss-green rug and hearth state kit\",\"set_asset\",\"Luan planned\",\"Authorship record pending creation\",\"Not created\",\"Domestic montage, fire origin and burned continuity\",\"not_created\",\"Bare, growing, final, burning and absent states.\"\n\"SET-002\",\"Crying-frame, anchor and baffle kit\",\"set_asset\",\"Luan planned\",\"Authorship record pending creation\",\"Not created\",\"Portal states and final chamber\",\"not_created\",\"Include asymmetry, ledge and protagonist-free aftermath.\"\n\"SET-003\",\"MATCH PATH ridge kit\",\"set_asset\",\"Luan planned\",\"Authorship record pending creation\",\"Not created\",\"Scenes 1, 2 and 10\",\"not_created\",\"R0 morning and R4 fire-night dressing around one camera.\"\n\"SET-004\",\"Granite seam and portal-foot reference kit\",\"continuity_asset\",\"Luan planned\",\"Authorship record pending creation\",\"Not created\",\"R0–R4 geography and marker absences\",\"not_created\",\"Measurements recorded only after build.\"\n\"SET-005\",\"Scene 13 vertical modules\",\"set_asset\",\"Luan planned\",\"Authorship record pending creation\",\"Not created\",\"Audience-only ascent\",\"not_created\",\"Stone, granite, soil and surface modules.\"\n\"AUDIO-001\",\"Narration master\",\"audio\",\"Luan planned\",\"Authorship and performer record pending\",\"Not recorded\",\"Third-person narration and exact Scene 2/13 reuse\",\"not_recorded\",\"No narration file exists.\"\n\"AUDIO-002\",\"Moss gate bark master\",\"audio_element\",\"No recording exists\",\"Source and rights not recorded\",\"Not recorded\",\"Scene 9 source and Scene 12 memory reuse\",\"not_recorded\",\"Must be one future performance placed twice.\"\n\"AUDIO-003\",\"Ambience and foley library\",\"audio\",\"Source not selected\",\"Source and licence not recorded\",\"Not selected\",\"Wind, rain, fire, work, steps, paws and room tone\",\"rights_pending\",\"Use original or verified licensed sources.\"\n\"MUSIC-001\",\"Restrained score elements\",\"music\",\"Source not selected\",\"Source and licence not recorded\",\"Not selected\",\"Limited montage and dramatic support\",\"rights_pending\",\"No music in Scene 1 or after Scene 12 death.\"\n\"VFX-001\",\"Echo portal treatment\",\"vfx_asset\",\"Luan planned\",\"Authorship record pending\",\"Not created\",\"Destination views, particles, failure and topology\",\"not_created\",\"Live rendering conditional on tests.\"\n\"VFX-002\",\"Fire, smoke, blast and delayed activation treatment\",\"vfx_asset\",\"Luan planned\",\"Authorship/source records pending\",\"Not created\",\"Scenes 1, 9, 10 and 12\",\"not_created\",\"Every third-party element requires provenance.\"\n\"GFX-001\",\"Title, journal, Atlas and ledger graphics\",\"graphic_asset\",\"Luan planned\",\"Font and authorship rights not recorded\",\"Not created\",\"Readable story information\",\"rights_pending\",\"Verify font rights and delivery-size legibility.\"\n\"STB-001\",\"Text-first storyboard pack\",\"planning_asset\",\"Luan planned\",\"Owned after approval\",\"49 planned panels; no images\",\"All thirteen scenes\",\"planned\",\"CSV and Markdown descriptions only.\"\n\"STB-002\",\"Later graphite-and-ink consistency test\",\"image_test\",\"Model and source screenshots not yet used\",\"Terms and provenance not yet recorded\",\"Not run\",\"Five reference-driven storyboard transformations\",\"not_started\",\"No generation is authorised by this plan.\""},{"path":".studio/internal/production/location-cards.csv","content":"location_id,name,story_function,hero_angle,modular_elements,lighting_state,completion,notes\n\"LOC-001\",\"MATCH PATH ridge and homestead approach\",\"Joins the R4 emergency to the lone R0 arrival and resumes the run in Scene 10\",\"MP-C locked view along path towards homestead\",\"Ridge path; cargo mark; distant homestead shell; smoke/fire layers; untouched R0 dressing\",\"R0 morning and R4 fire-night\",\"not_started\",\"One numerical camera, FOV, path centreline and travel direction; test CONT-001.\"\n\"LOC-002\",\"R0 clearing and overlook\",\"Earns the chosen home, survival chain and established pair before mining\",\"Wide water/birch overlook plus MF-A ravine-lip frame\",\"Fresh clearing; shelter stages; crops; cow pen; fishing bank; anvil area; Moss marks\",\"Morning, several Minecraft days, rain and MATCH FRAME A morning\",\"not_started\",\"Protagonist arrives alone; preserve wild, tamed-unnamed and named milestones.\"\n\"LOC-003\",\"Master ravine and granite-seam corridor\",\"Provides the shared coordinate and ordinary mining route across every echo\",\"Consistent seam profile with exposed iron visibly continuing around the turn\",\"Water descent; safe ledges; forked seam; iron vein; portal chamber; surface column\",\"Neutral master reference\",\"not_started\",\"Approve and protect before copying; actual seed and coordinates unselected.\"\n\"LOC-004\",\"R1 Rain Echo\",\"Confirms the visible rainy destination while disproving the surface-home assumption\",\"Matched seam arrival, portal parallax axis and empty surface footprint\",\"Waterfall; roof opening; dense growth; wet floor; single left-foot marker\",\"Fixed rainy day\",\"not_started\",\"Physical dressing must carry the distinction; test POC-004.\"\n\"LOC-005\",\"R2 Ash Echo\",\"Turns failed return into deliberate marker testing\",\"Exact frame-foot insert plus scorched surface geography\",\"Ash layer; scorched tree line; exposed shelf; bare arrival foot; L marker and outer torch\",\"Dry overcast late day\",\"not_started\",\"R1 marker absent; capture L state before crossing.\"\n\"LOC-006\",\"R3 Archive Echo\",\"Makes the older journal personal and forces the final uncontrolled crossing\",\"Compact desk/recess axis with portal and gravel stair in one wide\",\"Desk; protected drawer; familiar torch side; storage; ravine symbol; gravel states\",\"Dusk with readable inserts\",\"not_started\",\"Only seven Script-approved Atlas instructions; failing-mouth plates separate.\"\n\"LOC-007\",\"R4 fresh surface and first shelter\",\"Replaces travel with immediate shelter need\",\"Wide line connecting dead-mouth surface marker to first roof\",\"Clean water; timber; surface marker; first-roof modules; untouched approach\",\"Morning to first night\",\"not_started\",\"Preserve before homestead development.\"\n\"LOC-008\",\"R4 homestead, shared room and search routes\",\"Builds home, supplies the fire cause and presents unresolved absence\",\"Locked domestic HR-C frame and breached shortest-wall hero angle\",\"House milestones; stone hearth; rug states; timber route; removable wall; crops; ridge; hollow\",\"Seasonal passage, departure day, fire night and search dawn\",\"not_started\",\"Separate lived, pre-fire, burning and burned copies; test MEC-004 and EDIT-002.\"\n\"LOC-009\",\"R4 conventional portal approach\",\"Establishes repeatable supply routine and Scene 1 return direction\",\"Medium two-shot from gate towards rug return line\",\"Ordinary obsidian portal; small shelter edge; feed mark; sit-return path\",\"Day departure and night return direction\",\"not_started\",\"Visual and audio language distinct from echo frames.\"\n\"LOC-010\",\"R4 final frame chamber and creeper ledge\",\"Answers the portal mystery and stages fatal interruption\",\"FC-B wide showing frame, baffle, hero, landing space and dark ledge\",\"Incomplete/complete frame states; charged-anchor appearance; baffle; ledge; landing mark; protected journals; aftermath\",\"Day-to-night and smoky post-blast night\",\"not_started\",\"Sacrificial copies only; connected route required by MEC-005 and CONT-003.\"\n\"LOC-011\",\"Scene 13 vertical transition modules\",\"Links the active frame to MATCH FRAME A as omniscient presentation\",\"Fixed upward environmental axis through seam, stone, soil and surface\",\"Portal edge; granite module; stone layers; soil/root layer; surface opening\",\"Mine darkness into exact R0 morning\",\"not_started\",\"May be Blender or in-game modules; never protagonist viewpoint.\""},{"path":".studio/internal/production/location-plan.md","content":"# Location plan\n\n> Planned modular production design only. No seed, coordinate, world, structure or completed build is evidenced.\n\n## Hero location\n\nSelect one compact ridge–clearing–ravine column that can support all recurring geography. The approved master must contain, within practical loaded distance, the `MATCH PATH` approach, R0 overlook, fishing bank, ravine descent, forked granite seam, exposed-iron turn and portal chamber. The corresponding surface column must allow R1 vegetation/water dressing, R2 scorch dressing, R4 home construction and the Scene 13 ascent.\n\nUse one local survey origin at the portal-frame centre. Record actual world coordinates only after a candidate seed is created and visually approved. The seam must be recognisable from the portal approach and sit close enough to the surface column that an audience can understand the Scene 13 vertical relationship. Preserve an untouched master before placing any echo-specific block.\n\n## Modular build strategy\n\n### Terrain modules\n\n- Master ravine wall and forked seam: permanent reference geometry copied into every echo.\n- Replaceable roof opening and waterfall: R1 only.\n- Replaceable scorched shelf, tree silhouettes and ash emitters: R2 only.\n- Compact survey recess and gravel stair: R3 only.\n- Incomplete, complete, active and aftermath portal-chamber states: separate bounded modules.\n- Surface dressing rings: near-camera hero ring, midground identity ring and silhouette-only background ring.\n\n### Homestead modules\n\n- Fixed foundation and exterior silhouette around `MATCH PATH`.\n- Swappable wall/roof milestones for Scene 8.\n- Shared-room floor cassette containing bare, first-rug, final-rug, first-flame and burned-fan states.\n- Stone hearth kept on one invariant mark.\n- Removable shortest wall for Scene 10.\n- Independent furniture/storage dressing so forbidden items can be inspected before aftermath capture.\n\n### Lighting and access\n\nKeep a camera corridor behind every hero angle and hide incomplete surfaces outside the maximum tested FOV. Provide safe operator access behind the portal wall, shared-room camera wall and final-chamber baffle. Fix time/weather through the take controller; use physical torch placements as continuity anchors. Build ceilings only where visible or where portal/weather mechanics require them.\n\n### Surfaces that never need to exist\n\n- Full interiors behind unopened storage walls.\n- A complete Nether route; only the conventional portal approach and short material-return fragments are required.\n- A full Archive complex beyond the desk, storage and blocked stair.\n- Complete landscapes outside R1/R2 establishing wedges.\n- A continuous subterranean shaft for Scene 13 if modular dissolves communicate the route.\n\n## Perceived-scale cheats\n\n- Occlude horizon joins with ridge profiles, birch canopies and ravine walls.\n- Use rain, waterfall sound and dense near vegetation to make R1 feel wetter and larger without extending the playable area.\n- Use ash drift, a scorched silhouette card and a narrow exposed shelf to imply wider R2 damage.\n- Keep the R3 recess narrow so the unexplored darkness suggests more archive than is built.\n- Let conventional-portal audio, returning inventory and short threshold fragments imply repeated Nether journeys.\n- Use locked cutaways to crops, ridge, ravine, shelter and hollow to enlarge the R4 search without building new locations.\n- Use smoke and low-value silhouettes to conceal missing R4 fire-night background detail.\n- Use modular stone and soil layers with matched upward motion for Scene 13 rather than literal world clipping.\n\n## Build order\n\n1. Resolve the provisional stack and run R0/R1 proof tests in disposable worlds.\n2. Search for and approve the hero geography; record seam, surface column and camera-access constraints.\n3. Preserve the untouched master and verify restoration.\n4. Mark `MATCH PATH`, `MATCH FRAME A`, portal-parallax, frame-foot and final-chamber camera corridors.\n5. Build/capture R0 fresh arrival and survival milestones in causal order.\n6. Derive R1 and validate rain; derive R2/R3 only after live/composite portal selection.\n7. Derive fresh R4 and preserve it before shelter construction.\n8. Advance R4 through home milestones, preserving each rug and pre-fire state.\n9. Build fire and burned cassettes in copies; never burn the only lived room.\n10. Build the final chamber, baffle and physically connected creeper ledge in a sacrificial copy.\n11. Build the protagonist-free aftermath and Scene 13 modules after blast/composite tests.\n12. Perform a Script and continuity review before set lock.\n\n## Blender versus in-game split\n\nPrefer in-game terrain, character performances, block placement, ordinary portal, domestic states and all geography viewers must recognise as Minecraft. Use a live Immersive Portals view only after it passes.\n\nBlender or another compositor is provisional for portal cards and depth occlusion, smoke/particle layering, exact camera matching, the delayed activation and Scene 13’s modular ascent. It may also produce greyboxes for panels whose in-game set is not yet built. No exact Blender version or successful workflow is claimed.\n\n## Reuse after this video\n\nHigh-reuse elements are the master ravine shell, portal chamber, take-controller conventions, camera-mark system, structure-reset workflow, shared-room cassette, weathered-journal insert template and graphite storyboard style pack. Reuse must not overwrite this video’s protected milestones or imply that third-party rights have already been cleared."},{"path":".studio/internal/production/build-budget.md","content":"# Build budget\n\n> Planning estimate only. Hours are solo-production estimates, not logged labour. No cash purchase or commission is authorised. `Reuse value` uses 1–5, where 5 is broadly reusable.\n\n| Work package | Estimated hours | Cash cost | Reuse value | Must / should / could |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---|\n| Exact-version and dependency evidence | 12 | BRL 0 authorised | 4 | must |\n| R0/R1 portal, world and weather proof | 20 | BRL 0 authorised | 5 | must |\n| Datapack take-controller and reset rehearsal | 20 | BRL 0 authorised | 5 | must |\n| Camera, replay and capture comparison | 14 | BRL 0 authorised | 4 | must |\n| Master geography selection and continuity marks | 18 | BRL 0 authorised | 5 | must |\n| R0 survival and Moss-state builds | 22 | BRL 0 authorised | 3 | must |\n| R1–R3 modular echo dressing | 24 | BRL 0 authorised | 4 | must |\n| R4 shelter and homestead milestones | 28 | BRL 0 authorised | 5 | must |\n| Shared-room fire and burned-state cassettes | 18 | BRL 0 authorised | 5 | must |\n| Final frame, baffle, ledge and aftermath | 18 | BRL 0 authorised | 4 | must |\n| Journals, Atlas, ledger and title graphics | 18 | BRL 0 authorised | 4 | must |\n| Text-board greyboxing and animatic | 20 | BRL 0 authorised | 5 | must |\n| Essential portal, fire and Scene 13 composites | 24 | BRL 0 authorised | 4 | must |\n| Additional montage angles and background detail | 16 | BRL 0 authorised | 2 | should |\n| Optional shader/performance polish | 10 | BRL 0 authorised | 2 | could |\n| Later five-panel generated-sketch comparison | 6 | BRL 0 authorised | 3 | could |\n| Contingency for failed resets and pickups | 24 | BRL 0 authorised | 3 | should |\n\n## Totals and interpretation\n\n- Must packages: approximately 256 hours.\n- Should packages: approximately 40 hours.\n- Could packages: approximately 16 hours.\n- Full planning envelope: approximately 312 solo hours.\n- Authorised cash: BRL 0.\n\nNo software is assumed to be free merely because the authorised cash column is zero. Exact licences, prices and commercial-use terms remain evidence tasks. Any storage, subscription, asset, commission or contractor cost requires a current quote in BRL and human approval before commitment.\n\n## Cut line\n\nProtect every must package until all thirteen causal scenes have a feasible capture or composite route. If scope must shrink:\n\n1. Remove shaders and cosmetic rendering additions.\n2. Keep the text/greybox storyboard and omit the generated-sketch comparison.\n3. Reduce background dressing outside hero wedges.\n4. Reduce repeated montage coverage while retaining the taming/name chain, Moss routines, rug growth and material preparation.\n5. Replace the literal Scene 13 rise with shorter modular dissolves.\n\nDo not cut `MATCH PATH`, `MATCH FRAME A`, granite-seam recognition, either absent marker, the seven Atlas inserts, fire-origin evidence, the unresolved Moss search, Scene 11’s connected creeper plant, the fatal interruption or delayed R0 destination reveal.\n\nCustom-mod time and cash are outside this budget. They may be estimated only after a documented existing-tool failure and explicit human approval."},{"path":".studio/internal/production/risk-register.md","content":"# Risk register\n\n| Risk | Probability | Impact | Trigger | Mitigation | Fallback | Owner |\n|---|---:|---:|---|---|---|---|\n| Exact 1.21.1 comparison remains unsupported | High | Medium | No primary exact-release intersection is available | Run VER-121 before discussing migration | Keep provisional 1.20.1 baseline | Luan |\n| Loader or dependency chain is inferred rather than pinned | High | Blocker | Fabric, API or library release is selected without exact metadata | Complete VER-120 and record source, version, licence and constraints | Remove optional component or replace failed tool | Luan |\n| Portal, weather and multiple-world candidates do not operate together | Medium–High | Blocker | Launch failure, missing world, invalid destination or weather corruption | Add one component at a time in an isolated profile and reload after each | Composite destination and use shot-specific world states | Luan |\n| Multiworld states are not addressable as Immersive Portals dimensions | High | Blocker | Destination command cannot resolve a Multiworld world ID | Test destination registration before dressing echoes | Separately sourced custom dimensions, shot configurations or composites | Luan |\n| Asymmetric R4→R0 view and R0→R1 entry cannot coexist live | High | Blocker | R0 entry returns to R4 or another unintended destination | Record all faces/directions in POC-005 | Use shot-specific portal configurations or composites | Luan |\n| R1 weather is absent or incorrect through R0 opening | Medium | High | Rain, light or waterfall differs before and after crossing | Test without shaders with fixed states | Composite rainy R1 plate and rebuild audio | Luan |\n| Time/weather candidates overlap or conflict | Medium | High | Shared time, duplicated control or state corruption appears | Test Dimensional Weather and Dimension Level Data separately | Use fixed-time plates and one passing weather method | Luan |\n| Portal state changes after save/reload | Medium | High | Destination, shape or orientation changes | Record commands, orientation and IDs; repeat after reload | Rebuild shot portals from recorded setup or composite | Luan |\n| Portal performance is unstable | Medium–High | High | Frame spikes, chunk stalls or clipping occur | Preload required chunks, reduce recursion/distance and establish no-shader baseline | Capture foreground/destination separately | Luan |\n| Camera/replay tool fails to record portal or cross-world entities | High | High | Interior disappears, Moss is missing or replay corrupts | Compare Replay Mod and CinematicTools separately after baseline | Locked gameplay, spectator paths or matched plates | Luan |\n| Shaders obscure clues or destabilise capture | Medium | Medium–High | Seam, marker, rain or frame interior becomes unreadable | Test last and review at delivery size | Remove shaders; use vanilla lighting/post grade | Luan |\n| Recording tool, codec or hardware cannot hold usable pacing | Medium | High | Dropped/duplicated frames or corrupted output | Select settings through PERF-001 and inspect actual files | Lower settings, offline render or layered plates | Luan |\n| Datapack reset affects the wrong world or entities | Low–Medium | Blocker | Cleanup selector reaches persistent Moss or protected build | Require namespace plus take tag and display world/region before changes | Restore verified milestone and revise selector | Luan |\n| Structure restoration does not preserve portal or wolf state | Medium | High | Portal entities, owner data or block entities drift | Keep those systems outside untested structure assumptions | World/region milestone copies and explicit entity validation | Luan |\n| Clean master or sole milestone is contaminated | Medium | Blocker | Work is copied in the wrong direction or destructive capture reaches source | Read-only naming discipline and verified independent copies | Restore last verified master-derived copy | Luan |\n| Echo geography drifts | Low if controlled | High | Seam, cave or surface profile differs | Derive from one master and overlay references | Build a matched hero-location shell | Luan |\n| MATCH PATH drifts | Medium | High | Camera, FOV, light or path direction differs | Use one numerical camera and reference overlay | Rebuild visible dressing around one source plate | Luan |\n| MATCH FRAME A cannot be repeated | Medium | Blocker | Moss, kit, journal, light or pack timing differs | Protect the R0 established-pair state and one narration master | Reuse the Scene 2 source image/continuation where feasible | Luan |\n| Repeated narration is recorded twice | Low | High | Timing, inflection or room sound differs | Record once and place the same asset twice | Replace both placements from one approved master | Luan |\n| Granite seam becomes obscure or symbolic | Medium | Medium–High | Dressing hides the natural fork or narration overstates it | Preserve silhouette and stable screen position | Add a short neutral orientation insert | Luan |\n| Wild-wolf and skeleton action is unclear | Medium–High | High | Paths collide, targeting fails or collar appears early | Use marks and separate controlled plates | Join threat, intervention and taming editorially | Luan |\n| Fishing capture depends on uncontrolled luck | High | Medium | Schedule stalls or catch is unreadable | Plan controlled catch/pick-up insert while retaining fishing cause | Inventory insert joined to genuine fishing action | Luan |\n| Moss’s name, collar or owner state is wrong | Medium | High | Incorrect continuity state enters shot | Maintain separate wild, tamed-unnamed and named checks | Replace plate from correct protected state | Luan |\n| Moss fails portal crossing or reload | Medium–High | High | Duplication, loss, pose or owner change | Run MEC-003 before hero capture | Destination-side Moss plate with concealed handoff | Luan |\n| Fire does not follow the rug-to-timber route | High | Blocker | Spread stalls, accelerates or destroys evidence | Repeat tests from exact backed-up room | Progressive states with tested origin and approved burn fan | Luan |\n| Destructive capture destroys the only lived homestead | Medium | Blocker | Fire, wall break or blast begins without restore proof | Verify independent pre-fire and burned copies | Restore latest verified milestone | Luan |\n| Edit resolves Moss’s fate | Medium | High | Body, collar-like drop, death text or locating sound appears | Run EDIT-002 on every relevant plate and stem | Remove or replace offending evidence | Luan |\n| Creeper route is invisible or too obvious | Medium | Medium–High | Edge cannot be found on rewatch or acts as a reveal | Review sub-second plant at delivery size without sting | Adjust duration/contrast within Script restraint | Luan |\n| Creeper fall and hiss cannot hit timing | Medium–High | High | It misses, lands early or fails to ignite | Test route and cues separately with tagged actor | Separate glimpse, fall, landing, hiss and reaction plates | Luan |\n| Blast fails to kill protagonist or destroys all readable geometry | High | Blocker | Damage is insufficient or frame disappears | Test sacrificial chamber with recorded settings | Black fatal cut plus art-directed aftermath | Luan |\n| Aftermath items imply false evidence | Medium | High | Items include a tag, collar-like object or impossible inventory | Approve a restrained list and fixed marks | Remove items and use a simpler plate | Luan |\n| Delayed activation is mistaken for vanilla behaviour | Medium | High | Production/publication wording presents it as factual | Label it invented canon in every plan and review | Revise VFX and release language | Luan |\n| Atlas pages retain superseded direct-discharge wording | Medium | High | Page says the protagonist must discharge the anchor | Build pages from the seven Script labels only | Replace insert before picture lock | Luan |\n| Portal sound attracts R0 protagonist from surface | Medium | High | Hum appears in Scene 2 or Scene 13 surface audio | Keep isolated stems and full-sequence audio review | Rebuild underground-only sound in post | Luan |\n| Scene 13 suggests post-death consciousness | Medium | High | Camera begins at eye height or carries personal sound | Start on an external protagonist-free plate and use environmental movement | Shorter environmental dissolves | Luan |\n| Storyboard generation changes geometry or canon | High if unconstrained | Medium | Model invents props, characters, Moss evidence or camera angle | Reference-first five-panel test and overlays | Keep text/greybox boards only | Luan |\n| Third-party rights remain unclear | Medium | Blocker | Skin, font, sound, music, mod or plug-in enters use without evidence | Record exact source, owner, licence and permitted use | Replace with original or verified alternative | Luan |\n| Scope exceeds solo capacity | Medium–High | High | Full-world dressing, custom code or redundant coverage delays causal scenes | Enforce budget cut line and proof gates | Reduce cosmetic coverage and use modular plates | Luan |\n| Storage failure removes a world state or capture | Medium | Blocker | Sole copy corrupts or is overwritten | Verify working and independent backup copies before destructive work | Restore latest verified state and recapture | Luan |\n| A take is selected without evidence | Low | Blocker | Selection is recorded without an existing playable capture and review | Require actual file, technical inspection and human decision | Leave capture/selection records untouched | Luan |\n\n## Scope tripwires\n\n- Do not build all five echoes before POC-003 and POC-004 pass or yield an approved composite recipe.\n- Do not migrate to 1.21.1 without VER-121.\n- Do not commission or build a custom mod before an existing-tool test isolates a precise missing capability.\n- Do not use unrelated seeds.\n- Do not add shaders before the no-shader baseline is stable.\n- Do not capture direct anchor discharge as story action.\n- Do not add a surface portal hum in R0.\n- Do not burn, break or explode the only copy of a set state.\n- Do not use paid or uncleared assets without human approval; quote costs in BRL.\n- Stop after unexplained world, entity or portal corruption and preserve logs before changing versions.\n\n## Rights and recovery controls\n\n1. Obtain software only from recorded official project or release pages.\n2. Record exact artefact, version, source, licence and hash before use.\n3. Keep original configs, datapacks, graphics and builds separate from third-party binaries.\n4. Preserve clean profile, untouched master and verified milestones.\n5. Retain crash reports, logs, screenshots and concise reproduction notes for each blocker.\n6. Test changes on copies, never the sole production state."},{"path":".studio/internal/production/build-log.md","content":"# Build log\n\n## Build baseline\n\n**Evidence status:** Planning and supplied-source research only. No Minecraft profile, proof of concept, datapack, world, location, graphic, audio file, capture or storyboard image is evidenced.\n\n**Portal implementation status:** Research candidate. Immersive Portals 5.2.0, Multiworld 1.12 and independent weather candidates have documented individual 1.20.1 support; combined compatibility is untested.\n\n**Provisional baseline:** Minecraft Java Edition 1.20.1 with Fabric. Java, Fabric Loader/API, iCommon API and optional camera dependencies remain unpinned.\n\n**1.21.1 comparison:** Evidence gap. No exact supporting-release intersection is present in the supplied source set. This does not mean such releases do not exist.\n\n**World strategy:** Create one clean master and derive R0–R4 through verified copies or controlled regions. No seed or coordinate has been selected.\n\n**Script authority:** Production follows all thirteen scenes of `draft-03`. The protagonist does not ignite or directly discharge the final system; the creeper explodes first. Delayed activation is invented canon. R4 Moss’s fate remains unresolved.\n\n## Session log\n\n### 2026-07-15\n\n- Changes: Initial production planning files created.\n- Evidence/screenshots: None recorded.\n- Performance notes: Not measured.\n- Deviations: None implemented.\n- Next action: Research portal implementation.\n\n### 2026-07-16 — portal feasibility research handoff\n\n- Changes: Recorded supplied candidates for see-through portal travel, separate echo states, same-seed geography and independent weather; defined a proof gate and composite fallback.\n- Evidence/screenshots: Source records only. No in-game evidence.\n- Performance notes: Not measured.\n- Deviations: None implemented.\n- Decision: Do not commission a custom mod before a precise existing-tool failure is retained.\n- Next action: Resolve exact dependencies and run the minimum proof.\n\n### 2026-07-16 — Script-led production development\n\n- Changes: Planned thirteen scenes and established `MATCH PATH`, `MATCH FRAME A`, granite-seam, fire, creeper-route and delayed-activation controls.\n- Evidence/screenshots: None created.\n- Performance notes: Not measured.\n- Deviations: None implemented.\n- Decision: Script `draft-03` supersedes conflicting Story and Direction material.\n- Next action: Run the isolated R0-to-R1 baseline before full echo construction.\n\n### 2026-07-17 — research-first deepening proposal\n\n- Changes: Reorganised the supplied primary-source findings into an exact-version comparison; selected 1.20.1 as a provisional evidence-led baseline; recorded the absent 1.21.1 intersection; designed the datapack-first take controller; completed planning matrices, 49 text storyboard panels, camera paths, modular locations, budget and expanded risks.\n- Evidence/screenshots: No new external research, installation, test, build, capture or generated image is claimed. This entry records synthesis from supplied context only.\n- Performance notes: Not measured.\n- Deviations: None implemented.\n- Decision: Test one world, weather and camera method at a time. Keep live and composite portal routes available. Defer custom development.\n- Next action: Complete VER-120 and VER-121, then run POC-001.\n\n## Planned take-controller record\n\n**Status:** Designed, not implemented.\n\nPlanned lifecycle: `setup`, `arm`, `action`, `reset`, `cleanup`.\n\nPlanned controls: namespaced temporary tags; marker entities; `tpnm_take`, `tpnm_phase`, `tpnm_tick` and `tpnm_cue` objectives; fixed time/weather; disabled natural spawning; protected world/region restoration; explicit wild, tamed-unnamed and named Moss states; separate skeleton, fire and creeper plates.\n\nNo datapack file, command execution, state inspection or reset result exists.\n\n## Version research queue\n\n| Test | Requirement | Status | Next evidence |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| VER-120 | Pin Java, Fabric Loader/API, iCommon and conditional camera dependencies for 1.20.1 | `not_run` | Official exact release pages and dependency table |\n| VER-121 | Establish an exact 1.21.1 portal/world/weather/control/camera intersection | `not_run` | Official exact release pages or explicit absence record |\n\n## Portal proof-of-concept record\n\nRetain every completed run as a new subsection. Never replace earlier evidence.\n\n### Test POC-001 — not run\n\n- Date: Not run\n- Operator: Luan\n- Minecraft version: 1.20.1 candidate\n- Java version: Not recorded\n- Fabric Loader version: Not recorded\n- Fabric API artefact/version/hash: Not recorded\n- Immersive Portals artefact/version/hash: Not recorded\n- Other installed mods: None recorded\n- Test world seed: Not selected\n- World ID: Not created\n- Portal coordinates/orientation: Not selected\n- Resolution/frame-rate target: Not selected\n- GPU/driver: Not recorded\n\n| Check | Result | Evidence | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Clean profile launches | Not run | None | Minimum stack only |\n| Portal can be created | Not run | None | Record exact command/configuration |\n| Save and reload preserve portal | Not run | None | Repeat twice |\n| Static destination view renders | Not run | None | Inspect clipping |\n| Lateral parallax is correct | Not run | None | Four-block planned move |\n| Player crossing is usable | Not run | None | Inspect discontinuity |\n\n#### Outcome\n\n- Status: `not_run`\n- Approved stack: None\n- Rejected components: None\n- Fallback selected: None\n- Next action: Complete exact dependency evidence, then run the isolated test.\n\n### Tests POC-002 through POC-005 — not run\n\nNo world IDs, seeds, destinations, weather states, Moss crossings, asymmetric routes, save/reload results, logs or recordings exist. Procedures and criteria are in the test matrix.\n\n## Mechanics, continuity and effects queue\n\n| Test ID | Requirement | Status |\n|---|---|---|\n| ACT-001 | Repeatable setup–arm–action–reset–cleanup lifecycle | `not_run` |\n| MEC-001 | Skeleton threat, wild-wolf intervention and taming | `not_run` |\n| MEC-002 | Fishing, name tag, anvil and MOSS application | `not_run` |\n| MEC-003 | Moss states, routines and portal crossing | `not_run` |\n| MEC-004 | Rug-origin fire route and reset | `not_run` |\n| MEC-005 | Connected creeper route, fall and hiss | `not_run` |\n| MEC-006 | Fatal blast and readable aftermath | `not_run` |\n| VFX-001 | Portal failure and quiet collapse | `not_run` |\n| VFX-002 | Delayed flash, particles and destination view | `not_run` |\n| VFX-003 | Smoke, water, steam and fire continuity | `not_run` |\n| CONT-001 | MATCH PATH and MATCH FRAME A | `not_run` |\n| CONT-002 | Marker-foot and granite-seam continuity | `not_run` |\n| CONT-003 | Final-frame asymmetry and creeper geography | `not_run` |\n| AUD-001 | Exact narration/bark reuse and audio boundaries | `not_run` |\n| GFX-001 | Journal, Atlas, ledger and title readability | `not_run` |\n| EDIT-001 | Scene 13 omniscient reading | `not_run` |\n| EDIT-002 | Moss fate remains unresolved | `not_run` |\n| STB-001 | Five-panel image-model consistency comparison | `not_run` |\n\n## Set-lock review\n\n**Status:** Not ready.\n\nPortal method, dependency pins, world duplication, weather, controller, camera path, Moss transfer, destructive resets and composite fallbacks have not produced evidence. Full echo dressing and destructive R4 construction remain gated.\n\n## Completion evidence\n\n- Completed locations: None evidenced.\n- Completed builds: None evidenced.\n- Implemented controller: None.\n- Recorded mechanics tests: None.\n- Generated storyboard images: None.\n- Recorded captures: None.\n- Recorded audio: None.\n- Selected takes: None.\n- Technically usable selected takes: None.\n- Pickups: Undetermined.\n\nCapture-log and audio-capture-log remain untouched. No capture or take-selection entry may be created until a genuine file exists and receives technical and human review."}],"questions":[],"warnings":["The supplied source set contains no exact Minecraft 1.21.1 portal/world/weather/control/camera intersection. The plan records this as an evidence gap and does not infer either support or incompatibility.","Exact Java, Fabric Loader/API, iCommon API, GeckoLib, CreativeCore, Replay Mod, recording, Blender, Sodium and Iris versions remain unpinned.","Every proposed combined stack, portal topology, weather view, Moss transfer, fire route, creeper performance, blast state and camera workflow remains untested.","The ChatGPT Images 2.0 recommendation is provisional from the supplied official-source summary; no five-panel consistency test or storyboard image has been generated.","Capture-log, audio-capture-log, selected-take and technical-usability checks correctly remain blocked because no genuine capture evidence exists."]}
